n A.T.F. Lab', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conditt, Mark Anthony (1994-2018)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laboratories and Scientific Equipment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-01T14:24:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ali Watkins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ali', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Watkins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d864b91c-1b39-5ce7-a542-697171f67ddc', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d864b91c-1b39-5ce7-a542-697171f67ddc'}, {'abstract': 'David Tanis’s leek soufflé, Alison Roman’s vegetarian tortilla soup, Swedish meatballs: Let NYT Cooking help you plan your menu for the days ahead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/01/dining/what-to-cook-this-week-newsletter.html', 'snippet': 'David Tanis’s leek soufflé, Alison Roman’s vegetarian tortilla soup, Swedish meatballs: Let NYT Cooking help you plan your menu for the days ahead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. Happy Easter. I’m sorry to say this will be my last newsletter. I’ve renounced home cooking and intend to eat only what I can have delivered to my garret. I just can’t anymore with the pots and the pans and the steam and the heat and the endless shopping and cooking and cleaning up afterward, the relentless good humor and every day more new recipes to test and to champion, to discover, to cheer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/dining/12COOKING-VEGETARIANTORTILLASOUP1/12COOKING-VEGETARIANTORTILLASOUP1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/12/dining/12COOKING-VEGETARIANTORTILLASOUP1/12COOKING-VEGETARIANTORTILLASOUP1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/dining/12COOKING-VEGETARIANTORTILLASOUP1/12COOKING-VEGETARIANTORTILLASOUP1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/dining/12COOKING-VEGETARIANTORTILLASOUP1/12COOKING-VEGETARIANTORTILLASOUP1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/dining/12COOKING-VEGETARIANTORTILLASOUP1/12COOKING-VEGETARIANTORTILLASOUP1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/12/dining/12COOKING-VEGETARIANTORTILLASOUP1/12COOKING-VEGETARIANTORTILLASOUP1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/dining/12COOKING-VEGETARIANTORTILLASOUP1/12COOKING-VEGETARIANTORTILLASOUP1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Cook This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-01T14:30:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/784ae4f8-d5b3-5817-a6e2-6a04da4feba2', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/784ae4f8-d5b3-5817-a6e2-6a04da4feba2'}, {'abstract': 'Carl Hoffman’s “The Last Wild Men of Borneo” tells the stories of an environmental activist accepted by an indigenous tribe and a man who became one of the world’s most successful tribal-art collectors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/01/books/last-wild-men-of-borneo-carl-hoffman-interview.html', 'snippet': 'Carl Hoffman’s “The Last Wild Men of Borneo” tells the stories of an environmental activist accepted by an indigenous tribe and a man who became one of the world’s most successful tribal-art collectors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruno Manser and Michael Palmieri went to Borneo, the third-largest island on the planet, seeking different things. Starting in the mid-1980s, Manser, a Swiss traveler, decided to live with the Penan, an indigenous tribe that eventually accepted him as one of its own. After several years with the Penan, Manser became an outspoken critic of deforestation on the island, and he disappeared in 2000, presumed dead. Mr. Palmieri, a Californian, eventually settled in Bali, and from there took a series of trips to Borneo seeking art and artifacts that he sold to museums and collectors. In “The Last Wild Men of Borneo,” Carl Hoffman, himself an adventurer-journalist, tells their stories. Like Manser and Mr. Palmieri, Hoffman has long harbored a fascination with Borneo. Its “forest and its people were the very definition of exotic in the Western mind,” he writes. Mr. Hoffman’s 2014 book, “Savage Harvest,” was an account of the disappearance of Nelson Rockefeller’s son Michael in New Guinea. Below, Mr. Hoffman discusses how that book led to this one, the way his view of his subjects changed over time and more.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/books/02hoffman1/02hoffman1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 865, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/books/02hoffman1/02hoffman1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 865}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/books/02hoffman1/02hoffman1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 711, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/books/02hoffman1/02hoffman1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1421, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/books/02hoffman1/02hoffman1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/books/02hoffman1/02hoffman1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/books/02hoffman1/02hoffman1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tell Us 5 Things About Your Book: Two Adventurers on Very Different Missions to Borneo', 'kicker': 'Q. & A.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Magnet in the Pacific', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Last Wild Men of Borneo: A True Story of Death and Treasure (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffman, Carl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Borneo (Indonesia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-01T15:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/9702744d-4903-5b37-83cf-3d93ba795caf', 'word_count': 1008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9702744d-4903-5b37-83cf-3d93ba795caf'}, {'abstract': 'In an era in which breaking news is relentless, how many push alerts are too many?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/01/insider/how-to-push-a-story.html', 'snippet': 'In an era in which breaking news is relentless, how many push alerts are too many?', 'lead_paragraph': '“Two white police officers in Baton Rouge, La., will not be prosecuted in the fatal 2016 shooting of Alton Sterling, a black man.” That was the text in a push notification that arrived on lock screens across the country on Tuesday, sent by The New York Times. Many had been awaiting the decision for years; the alert, one of several hundreds The Times will send this year, took readers straight to the breaking news on nytimes.com.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': N