of many parallels linking Mr. Wallace, remembered for conservatism and opposition to integration, to the trajectory of Donald J. Trump.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Separated by as much as half a century, the two men’s public lives run strikingly parallel. It’s as if they drank from the same political cup: George C. Wallace, the Alabama governor who ached to become president, and Donald J. Trump, the developer and showman who made it to the top. They are bound by their streaks of opportunism and by their campaigns tailored to resentful voters brimming with the conviction that society’s deck is stacked against them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'George Wallace Tapped Into Racial Fear. Decades Later, Its Force Remains Potent.', 'kicker': 'Retro Report', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Segregation and Desegregation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 1968', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights Movement (1954-68)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wallace, George C', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ayres, B Drummond Jr', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Southern States (US)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-01T22:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Na