 little remembrances, ideas about what constitutes a loving family, what makes a man. One of the essays describes the day his mother died.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/02millnerWEB/merlin_56038429_70411680-cfbc-406e-8ca7-0a731473dda2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/02millnerWEB/merlin_56038429_70411680-cfbc-406e-8ca7-0a731473dda2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/02millnerWEB/merlin_56038429_70411680-cfbc-406e-8ca7-0a731473dda2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/02millnerWEB/merlin_56038429_70411680-cfbc-406e-8ca7-0a731473dda2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/02millnerWEB/02millnerWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/02millnerWEB/02millnerWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/02millnerWEB/02millnerWEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Black American Dream', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Black American Dream', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-01T23:03:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denene Millner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Millner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/87c4096e-a804-5444-935b-60745da085ee', 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87c4096e-a804-5444-935b-60745da085ee'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees chose to pitch to Smoak instead of Josh Donaldson in the eighth inning, a decision that led to a game-changing home run for Toronto.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/01/sports/justin-smoak-yankees-blue-jays.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees chose to pitch to Smoak instead of Josh Donaldson in the eighth inning, a decision that led to a game-changing home run for Toronto.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TORONTO — With Toronto Blue Jays at second and third, two outs in the eighth inning and the Yankees clinging to a one-run lead, Manager Aaron Boone and the pitching coach Larry Rothschild looked to the mound from their perch on the dugout railing and gestured to reliever David Robertson.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/sports/02yankeesweb1/merlin_136278678_e9fd5f29-12b9-4058-a4f2-5534bcf58b9e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_n