ooking to buy a Kel-Tec Sub-2000, and I had one for sale. Other than that, I didn’t know him from Adam except for a few messages back and forth on Facebook.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '48', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/08mag-guns-image3/08mag-guns-image3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/08mag-guns-image3/08mag-guns-image3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/08mag-guns-image3/08mag-guns-image3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/08mag-guns-image3/08mag-guns-image3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/08mag-guns-image3/08mag-guns-image3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/08mag-guns-image3/08mag-guns-image3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/08mag-guns-image3/08mag-guns-image3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gun Culture Is My Culture. And I Fear for What It Has Become.', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At the Crossroads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parkland, Fla, Shooting (2018)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'APPALACHIAN REGION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunting and Trapping', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-02T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Joy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Joy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ad767be-3a1c-5c35-8723-2ada9a011f24', 'word_count': 4879, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ad767be-3a1c-5c35-8723-2ada9a011f24'}, {'abstract': 'On a trip from Iraqi Kurdistan to Sinjar, Alissa J. Rubin encountered an unsettling number of checkpoints that made travel nearly impossible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/02/magazine/iraq-sinjar-checkpoints-militias.html', 'snippet': 'On a trip from Iraqi Kurdistan to Sinjar, Alissa J. Rubin encountered an unsettling number of checkpoints that made travel nearly impossible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few American reporters have spent more time reporting from Iraq in the last 15 years than Alissa J. Rubin, who served as both a correspondent and the Baghdad bureau chief for The New York Times at the height of the conflict. Rubin returned to Iraq in 2014 to cover the rise of the Islamic State and was severely injured in a helicopter crash on Mount Sinjar while reporting on targeted attacks against the Yazidi population. She once again returned to the region in January 2018 for a coming article in The Times Magazine. On a drive to the Iraq-Syria border during her last trip, Rubin found that competing military and militia groups had set up checkpoints everywhere, making travel increasingly difficult. The following is an account of the nine hours it took her and her companions to drive 130 miles through more than 26 checkpoints.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29CHECKPOINT/merlin_136198107_8a9cd2cb-b9b5-47e0-af96-29d65e62ce69-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29CHECKPOINT/merlin_136198107_8a9cd2cb-b9b5-47e0-af96-29d65e62ce69-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29CHECKPOINT/merlin_136198107_8a9cd2cb-b9b5-47e0-af96-29d65e62ce69-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29CHECKPOINT/merlin_136198107_8a9cd2cb-b9b5-47e0-af96-29d65e62ce69-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29CHECKPOINT/29CHECKPOINT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29CHECKPOINT/29CHECKPOINT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29CHECKPOINT/29CHECKPOINT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Iraq, I Found Checkpoints as Endless as the Whims of Armed Men', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yazidi (Religious Sect)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sinjar (Iraq)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Iraqi Army', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Popular Mobilization Forces (Iraq)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pesh Merga', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-02T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/582e2687-f455-551d-9aab-00f9e5ef4d7d', 'word_count': 1825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/582e2687-f455-551d-9aab-00f9e5ef4d7d'}, {'abstract': 'A real estate developer-in-training finds a home in Hudson Yards, the largest construction site in the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/02/realestate/would-be-developer-hudson-yards-manhattan.html', 'snippet': 'A real estate developer-in-training finds a home in Hudson Yards, the largest construction site in the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When touring a potential apartment, many New Yorkers would be alarmed to see a construction shed next door, let alone a demolition site in the backyard. But Jeremy Vieira wasn’t the least bit concerned when his broker took him to see an apart