018/04/02/dining/worlds-fare-food-festival.html', 'snippet': 'A festival featuring 100 chefs, food vendors and restaurants hits the Citi Field parking lot on April 28 and 29.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An enormous, globally diverse food festival called World’s Fare, which is meant to recall the world’s fairs that were held in Flushing, Queens, decades ago, will move into the parking lot of Citi Field this month. Some culinary heavy-hitters like Claus Meyer, Jessica B. Harris and the street food expert K.F. Seetoh of Singapore are helping to set the lineup of 100 or so chefs, food vendors and restaurants that will participate. Craft breweries, art and music are part of it. Tickets, from $19 to $199 are now available: World’s Fare, April 28 and 29, 11 a.m. to 8 p.m., Citi Field, 123-01 Roosevelt Avenue, Flushing, Queens; theworldsfare.nyc.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerfare/merlin_136045764_016a2fbe-bccb-495b-8cc4-e1d6f775dc2a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 790, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerfare/merlin_136045764_016a2fbe-bccb-495b-8cc4-e1d6f775dc2a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 790}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerfare/merlin_136045764_016a2fbe-bccb-495b-8cc4-e1d6f775dc2a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 778, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerfare/merlin_136045764_016a2fbe-bccb-495b-8cc4-e1d6f775dc2a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1481, 'width': 1125, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerfare/04burnerfare-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerfare/04burnerfare-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerfare/04burnerfare-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Another World’s Fair Heads to Queens, This One for Foodies', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Gather: Yes, a Food Festival Is Coming to Queens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meyer, Claus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Street Fairs and Festivals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flushing (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Jessica B', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seetoh, K F', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-02T16:54:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/646773c1-2b84-5e59-9af6-bae6641f60af', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/646773c1-2b84-5e59-9af6-bae6641f60af'}, {'abstract': 'Delmonico’s will offer a special menu to mark the 150th anniversary of the day it welcomed women unescorted by men.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/02/dining/womens-rights-delmonicos.html', 'snippet': 'Delmonico’s will offer a special menu to mark the 150th anniversary of the day it welcomed women unescorted by men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a time when New York was more like Riyadh, in that a woman could not enter restaurants unaccompanied by a man. The rule was followed throughout the country. Then in 1868, Delmonico’s, the historic financial district restaurant, tossed it aside and welcomed women to a luncheon held by the Sorosis Club, a pioneering professional women’s organization. To mark the 150th anniversary of the event, the restaurant will feature a special menu created by Gabrielle Hamilton, the chef and owner of Prune, with dishes like beef bouillon with Madeira, a cheese fritter called Malakoff with salad, soft shell crabs with asparagus and américain sauce, and brûléed rice pudding, which will be served in addition to the regular lunch and dinner menus: Ladies’ Lunch, April 23 through 28, Delmonico’s, 56 Beaver Street (South William Street), 212-509-1144, delmonicosrestaurant.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerdelmonicos/merlin_111898211_7a9396d7-b105-4415-be45-54572f282266-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 491, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerdelmonicos/merlin_111898211_7a9396d7-b105-4415-be45-54572f282266-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 491}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerdelmonicos/merlin_111898211_7a9396d7-b105-4415-be45-54572f282266-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 837, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerdelmonicos/merlin_111898211_7a9396d7-b105-4415-be45-54572f282266-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1674, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerdelmonicos/04burnerdelmonicos-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerdelmonicos/04burnerdelmonicos-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerdelmonicos/04burnerdelmonicos-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Historic Women’s Luncheon Celebrates an Anniversary', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Celebrate: On Delmonico’s Menu, A Women’s Luncheon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Delmonico's", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prune (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Gabrielle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-02T16:58:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7ad2faf-1cb2-57c8-a0dd-a1b2d699f917', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7ad2faf-1cb2-57c8-a0dd-a1b2d699f917'}, {'abstract': '“Pizzapedia: An Illustrated Guide to Everyone’s Favorite Food” by Dan Bransfield is a lighthearted and well-researched guide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/02/dining/dan-bransfield-pizzapedia.html', 'snippet': '“Pizzapedia: An Illustrated Guide to Everyone’s Favorite Food” by Dan Bransfield is a lighthearted and well-researched guide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lighthearted yet well researched, this illustrated pizza Baedeker hits the right buttons. After a rundown on the history dating to the Roman era, it highlights pizza’s Neapolitan roots, Margherita of Savoy and the classic pizza named for her, and Lombardi’s in New York in 1905. It shows slices from today’s New York spots, including Di Fara, Emmy Squared and Patsy’s, and signature pizzas from several cities, including Chicago and Detroit. Tools, ingredients and futuristic pizza from drones, robots and vending machines are also covered: “Pizzapedia: An Illustrated Guide to Everyone’s Favorite Food” by Dan Bransfield (Ten Speed Press, $16)', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerpizza/04burnerpizza-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerpizza/04burnerpizza-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 356}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerpizza/04burnerpizza-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 607, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerpizza/04burnerpizza-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1215, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerpizza/04burnerpizza-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerpizza/04burnerpizza-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerpizza/04burnerpizza-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pizza, From Neapolitan Roots to Delivery Drones', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Consult: Pizza, Pizza, Pizza: Past, Present, Future', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pizza', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Pizzapedia: An Illustrated Guide to Everyone's Favorite Food (Book)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bransfield, Dan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-02T17:02:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d4b4b39-b5f4-5336-ac0e-b628d6afea22', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d4b4b39-b5f4-5336-ac0e-b628d6afea22'}, {'abstract': 'For the Bushwick Tea company, its beverage of choice should not take a back seat to coffee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/02/dining/tea-brooklyn-bushwick.html', 'snippet': 'For the Bushwick Tea company, its beverage of choice should not take a back seat to coffee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ratesh Chopra, whose fledgling tea company is rooted in Brooklyn, describes it as a “passion project.” Dissatisfied with how tea is often an afterthought where coffee is served, he decided to start his own company. By trial and error, he now has a growing inventory sold online and, increasingly, in local shops. He has eight varieties available online, including the black Brooklyn Breakfast, the well-balanced Moroccan Mint and some for making iced tea, with more to come. The teas are full leaf and come in silky sachets. I’m already hooked on the eye-opening Ginger & Turmeric, at once soothing and bold. Prices start at $12 for 15 tea bags: bushwicktea.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerteasub/04burnerteasub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 453, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerteasub/04burnerteasub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 453}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerteasub/04burnerteasub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerteasub/04burnerteasub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1546, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerteasub/04burnerteasub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerteasub/04burnerteasub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerteasub/04burnerteasub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Moving Tea to the Forefront in Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Brew: Giving Tea Its Props By Way of Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chopra, Ratesh', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bushwick Tea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bushwick (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-02T17:14:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58b7d90c-bfd6-5643-878b-6e7f4a1bf9cc', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58b7d90c-bfd6-5643-878b-6e7f4a1bf9cc'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Couch spent 720 days in jail after killing four people and paralyzing a fifth in a car crash. His defense contended that he was too rich to know right from wrong.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/02/us/ethan-couch-affluenza-jail.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Couch spent 720 days in jail after killing four people and paralyzing a fifth in a car crash. His defense contended that he was too rich to know right from wrong.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ethan Couch, whose trial for killing four people while driving drunk sparked widespread conversations about the privilege of being raised wealthy, was released from a Texas jail on Monday after nearly two years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/us/03affluenza_xp/03affluenza_xp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/us/03affluenza_xp/03affluenza_xp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/us/03affluenza_xp/03affluenza_xp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/us/03affluenza_xp/03affluenza_xp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/us/03affluenza_xp/03affluenza_xp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/us/03affluenza_xp/03affluenza_xp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/us/03affluenza_xp/03affluenza_xp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ethan Couch, ‘Affluenza Teen’ Who Killed 4 While Driving Drunk, Is Freed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Couch, Ethan (1997- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drunken and Reckless Driving', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Couch, Tonya (1967- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tarrant County (Tex)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-02T17:18:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Express', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Victor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Victor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7050eb6f-8bb2-54be-a524-766f71959abf', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7050eb6f-8bb2-54be-a524-766f71959abf'}, {'abstract': 'The Socarrat paella bars serve a tasty version of the drink called the Classico, with juniper berries and bitters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/02/dining/drinks/gin-tonic-socarrat.html', 'snippet': 'The Socarrat paella bars serve a tasty version of the drink called the Classico, with juniper berries and bitters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As we enter gin and tonic season, here’s a new way to enjoy the typical cooler. This version, called the Classico, is served at Socarrat, a group of paella restaurants, Spain being a country that’s mad for gin and tonic. It’s a beauty, served in a big stemmed wine goblet, not the usual highball glass, to give the components more room to mingle. Pour 2 ounces (or maybe more) of gin over ice cubes that half-fill the glass, add eight juniper berries, a couple of dashes of Angostura bitters, and the peel, in strips, of half a lemon. Stir well to chill, top with four ounces of cold high-quality tonic water, stir again and enjoy the sunset.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerginandtonic/merlin_136040811_b4c158cf-f0a7-4cab-82fd-e951011bb25f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerginandtonic/merlin_136040811_b4c158cf-f0a7-4cab-82fd-e951011bb25f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerginandtonic/merlin_136040811_b4c158cf-f0a7-4cab-82fd-e951011bb25f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerginandtonic/merlin_136040811_b4c158cf-f0a7-4cab-82fd-e951011bb25f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerginandtonic/04burnerginandtonic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerginandtonic/04burnerginandtonic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/dining/04burnerginandtonic/04burnerginandtonic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'widt