ly told story of history, science and reportage about the largest source of freshwater in the world, and the threat to America’s waterways. Become a member of the book club by joining our Facebook group, or by signing up to our newsletter. Learn more about the book club here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/books/02nowreadthis-egan-cover/02nowreadthis-egan-cover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 499, 'width': 347, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/books/02nowreadthis-egan-cover/02nowreadthis-egan-cover-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 499, 'width': 347, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/books/02nowreadthis-egan-cover/02nowreadthis-egan-cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/books/02nowreadthis-egan-cover/02nowreadthis-egan-cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/books/02nowreadthis-egan-cover/02nowreadthis-egan-cover-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Discussion Questions for ‘The Death and Life of the Great Lakes’', 'kicker': 'Now Read This', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Clubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Egan, Daniel P (1967- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Lakes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Death and Life of the Great Lakes (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-02T22:02:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8b5d1ee-bddc-5307-a2ea-600915939c9e', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8b5d1ee-bddc-5307-a2ea-600915939c9e'}, {'abstract': 'For years, caravans of immigrants have headed north from Central America. Despite Mr. Trump’s ominous tweets, many do not seek entry to in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/02/world/americas/caravans-migrants-mexico-trump.html', 'snippet': 'For years, caravans of immigrants have headed north from Central America. Despite Mr. Trump’s ominous tweets, many do not seek entry to in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEXICO CITY — It has become a regular occurrence, particularly around the Easter holiday: scores or even hundreds of Central American migrants making their way north by foot and vehicle from southern Mexico. They include everyone from infants to the elderly, fleeing violence and poverty in their homelands.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Transforms Immigrant Caravans in Mexico Into Cause Célèbre', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Huddled Masses Northbound Into Mexico Prompt Trump Alarm: ‘Caravans’ Coming', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asylum, Right of', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oaxaca (Mexico)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Honduras', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-02T22:05:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Semple', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Semple', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/adf28467-0834-5400-82e3-c0262dca1a49', 'word_count': 1123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adf28467-0834-5400-82e3-c0262dca1a49'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Tree, a violist, helped create the group in 1964. With only one change in its lineup, it performed for the next 45 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/02/obituaries/michael-tree-a-founder-of-the-guarneri-quartet-dies-at-84.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Tree, a violist, helped create the group in 1964. With only one change in its lineup, it performed for the next 45 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Tree, a founding member of the Guarneri String Quartet, the remarkably long-lived group that helped rekindle interest in chamber music in the 1960s and ’70s and continued to perform until 2009, died on Friday at his home in Manhattan. He was 84.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/obituaries/04tree-obit-1/tree-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/04/obituaries/04tree-obit-1/tree-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {