 and One Nights” reminds us that there have always been unreliable narrators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stories are shape shifters, as mutable and capricious as genies, in “Pay No Attention to the Girl,” Target Margin Theater’s timely gloss on the rich and strange ancient tales known as “The One Thousand and One Nights.” We are never allowed to forget that the multicolored narratives in this tantalizing production have constantly been redyed by the who, where and when of their telling during many centuries.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/theater/03paynoattention/merlin_136158303_f06186d8-5b81-4f9a-a96b-0a6ccf5ef51c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/theater/03paynoattention/merlin_136158303_f06186d8-5b81-4f9a-a96b-0a6ccf5ef51c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/theater/03paynoattention/merlin_136158303_f06186d8-5b81-4f9a-a96b-0a6ccf5ef51c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/theater/03paynoattention/merlin_136158303_f06186d8-5b81-4f9a-a96b-0a6ccf5ef51c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/theater/03paynoattention/03paynoattention-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/theater/03paynoattention/03paynoattention-th