y Stages production, Sharon Washington recalls how a magical period in her family’s history was also tinged with pain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For library lovers and assorted bibliophiles, the set of Sharon Washington’s solo show, “Feeding the Dragon,” at the Cherry Lane Theater, is a geeky pleasure — long, neat rows of colorful books; card catalogs along the edges; big multipaned windows above gleaming hardwood floors. To anyone who feels most at home surrounded by things to read, it feels like an invitation: Want to hear a story? Yes, please.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/07/theater/07feedingthedragonSKYBOX1/merlin_136204152_fe44b0ac-294f-4d36-9011-6a8192542d8b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/07/theater/07feedingthedragonSKYBOX1/merlin_136204152_fe44b0ac-294f-4d36-9011-6a8192542d8b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/07/theater/07feedingthedragonSKYBOX1/merlin_136204152_fe44b0ac-294f-4d36-9011-6a8192542d8b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/07/theater/07feedingthedragonSKYBOX1/merlin_136204152_fe44b0ac-294f-4d36-9011-6a8192542d8b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/07/theater/07feedingthedragonSKYBOX1/merlin_136204152_fe44b0ac-294f-4d36-9011-6a8192542d8b-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/07/theater/07feedingthedragonSKYBOX1/merlin_136204152_fe44b0ac-294f-4d36-9011-6a8192542d8b-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/07/theater/07feedingthedragonSKYBOX1/merlin_136204152_fe44b0ac-294f-4d36-9011-6a8192542d8b-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Feeding the Dragon,’ an Enchanted Home Inside a Library', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Enchanted Home Inside a Library', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Feeding the Dragon (Play)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Washington, Sharon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Primary Stages Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mileaf, Maria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-04T20:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Collins-Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins-Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d370a9e2-dcc8-5f46-b708-d9e2a46d9e34', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d370a9e2-dcc8-5f46-b708-d9e2a46d9e34'}, {'abstract': 'Revelations that digital consultants to the Trump campaign misused the data of millions of Facebook users set off a furor on both sides of the Atlantic. This is how The Times covered it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/04/us/politics/cambridge-analytica-scandal-fallout.html', 'snippet': 'Revelations that digital consultants to the Trump campaign misused the data of millions of Facebook users set off a furor on both sides of the Atlantic. This is how The Times covered it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In March, The New York Times, working with The Observer of London and The Guardian, obtained a cache of documents from inside Cambridge Analytica, the data firm principally owned by the right-wing donor Robert Mercer. The documents proved that the firm, where the former Trump aide Stephen K. Bannon was a board member, used data improperly obtained from Facebook to build voter profiles. The news put Cambridge under investigation and thrust Facebook into its biggest crisis ever. Here’s a guide to our coverage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/03/21/business/00cambridgestory6/merlin_135756423_8ac3aeb6-7781-4912-b9e5-fd7210e35170-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/03/21/business/00cambridgestory6/merlin_135756423_8ac3aeb6-7781-4912-b9e5-fd7210e35170-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/03/21/business/00cambridgestory6/merlin_135756423_8ac3aeb6-7781-4912-b9e5-fd7210e35170-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/03/21/business/00cambridgestory6/merlin_135756423_8ac3aeb6-7781-4912-b9e5-fd7210e35170-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/03/21/business/00cambrid