ashion/05LIZA1/05LIZA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Liza Minnelli Goes Marie Kondo; Old Holdings to Be Shown and Sold', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Warhol! ‘Cabaret’! Halston! Liza’s Past in ‘Castaways’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Costumes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Orderliness and Clutter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Halston (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Minnelli, Liza', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Minnelli, Vincente', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garland, Judy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-04T20:39:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank DeCaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DeCaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd05fc16-6fed-541b-bf0c-648f6d1896e2', 'word_count': 1092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd05fc16-6fed-541b-bf0c-648f6d1896e2'}, {'abstract': 'The pussy willow flowers early in New York City, giving butterflies and bumblebees their first sweet drink of the season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/04/nyregion/spring-arrives-on-kittens-paws.html', 'snippet': 'The pussy willow flowers early in New York City, giving butterflies and bumblebees their first sweet drink of the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The buds of pussy willow are a welcome communiqué from friendlier, warmer months ahead. Waving in the wind, they represent the spring we all imagine, beautiful and productive. Though these buds had been tucked into watertight protective scales all winter, by the middle of March, they have swollen to their maximum girth. By now, the earliest have begun to burst open in all their hairy glory, and by the first or second week of April they are in full flower.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/nyregion/08nature/merlin_105332149_a264de9e-c045-433a-97a5-8c260ce9e316-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/08/nyregion/08nature/merlin_105332149_a264de9e-c045-433a-97a5-8c260ce9e316-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/nyregion/08nature/merlin_105332149_a264de9e-c045-433a-97a5-8c260ce9e316-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/nyregion/08nature/merlin_105332149_a264de9e-c045-433a-97a5-8c260ce9e316-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/nyregion/08nature/merlin_105332149_a264de9e-c045-433a-97a5-8c260ce9e316-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/08/nyregion/08nature/merlin_105332149_a264de9e-c045-433a-97a5-8c260ce9e316-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/nyregion/08nature/merlin_105332149_a264de9e-c045-433a-97a5-8c260ce9e316-thumbL