an, Poland’s Kaczynski and Russia’s Putin among its proud members.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/05/opinion/viktor-orban-hungary-election.html', 'snippet': 'The Hungarian prime minister is a leader of an international reactionary movement that counts Turkey’s Erdogan, Poland’s Kaczynski and Russia’s Putin among its proud members.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday, Viktor Orban’s Fidesz party will likely cruise to another victory in Hungary’s general election, giving Mr. Orban, the reigning champion of “illiberal democracy” — a term he proudly embraces — a fourth term to pursue his assault on democratic institutions, immigrants, the European Union and anything smacking of social change. The campaign has been surprisingly tough, but then Fidesz designed the voting system and controls much of the media.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/opinion/04Orban-edt/merlin_136383774_c3897650-9587-4dac-aca3-1fb727c36d0b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/04/opinion/04Orban-edt/merlin_136383774_c3897650-9587-4dac-aca3-1fb727c36d0b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/opinion/04Orban-edt/merlin_136383774_c3897650-9587-4dac-aca3-1fb727c36d0b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/opinion/04Orban-edt/merlin_136383774_c3897650-9587-4dac-aca3-1fb727c36d0b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1537, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 