t', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flea Markets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Old Barracks Museum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Philip D (1957- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Washington, George (1732-99)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Trenton (NJ)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-05T15:14:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Besonen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Besonen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c03b8f4a-9c16-5f97-ad61-0bf5fec535e8', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c03b8f4a-9c16-5f97-ad61-0bf5fec535e8'}, {'abstract': 'More than two years after a Rutgers philosophy professor was convicted of raping a mentally disabled man, the central questions of the case remain unresolved.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/05/magazine/the-strange-case-of-anna-stubblefield-revisited.html', 'snippet': 'More than two years after a Rutgers philosophy professor was convicted of raping a mentally disabled man, the central questions of the case remain unresolved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent Monday in a crowded Newark courthouse, the former Rutgers philosophy professor Anna Stubblefield admitted she touched the penis of a man with cerebral palsy who could not legally consent. In an earlier trial, which I wrote about for The Times Magazine in October 2015, Anna was convicted on two counts of raping the same victim; last summer, that verdict was overturned on appeal. Her guilty plea has now forestalled a second trial, and barring some surprise at the sentencing in early May, she will receive no further time in prison beyond the nearly 22 months she has already served. It seems that this long, complicated story has come to a demoralizing end.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/magazine/04mag-stubblefield1/04mag-stubblefield1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/04/magazine/04mag-stubblefield1/04mag-stubblefield1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/magazine/04mag-stubblefield1/04mag-stubblefield1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/magazine/04mag-stubblefield1/04mag-stubblefield1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/magazine/04mag-stubblefield1/04mag-stubblefield1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/04/magazine/04mag-stubblefield1/04mag-stubblefield1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/04/magazine/04mag-stubblefield1/04mag-stubblefield1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Strange Case of Anna Stubblefield, Revisited', 'kicker': None, 'content_ki