gured out a key riddle in “2001: A Space Odyssey.” The actor who played the scene wasn’t so sure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is tempting to think that a work of great art appears in the material world complete and perfectly formed, like a rainbow or an egg, that every note or phrase or scene or brush stroke has been placed just so and for good reason. It is tempting to think that geniuses know what they are doing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/opinion/05handy/05handy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 891, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/05/opinion/05handy/05handy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 891}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/opinion/05handy/05handy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 690, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/opinion/05handy/05handy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1379, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/opinion/05handy/05handy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/05/opinion/05handy/05handy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/opinion/05handy/05handy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sometimes a Broken Glass Is Just a Broken Glass', 'k