', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONASAO, Central African Republic — Each morning, Marie Noella Kango walks over to the local clinic here and takes her spot behind the main desk by 8 a.m. Often, mothers and their children are already waiting in a line outside. One by one, the mothers meet with Ms. Kango and describe their children’s symptoms: fever, diarrhea, vomiting and stomach pains. These are all symptoms Ms. Kango can easily diagnose as malaria or parasites, the two most common ailments in this village. Then she prescribes a treatment plan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/06/opinion/06pagerWeb/merlin_135736779_e7d4a10a-24a6-4654-ab45-71aa3dbc92e9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/06/opinion/06pagerWeb/merlin_135736779_e7d4a10a-24a6-4654-ab45-71aa3dbc92e9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/06/opinion/06pagerWeb/merlin_135736779_e7d4a10a-24a6-4654-ab45-71aa3dbc92e9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/06/opinion/06pagerWeb/merlin_135736779_e7d4a10a-24a6-4654-ab45-71aa3dbc92e9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/06/opinion/06pagerWeb/06pagerWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/06/opinion/06pagerWeb/06pagerWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight