-palestinian-protest-israel.html', 'snippet': 'Though the protest and casualties were smaller than those last week, they made a point: portraying Gaza as a prison with Israel as the jailer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAHAL OZ, Israel — With tear gas and burning tires fouling the air and gunfire periodically ringing out from one direction, Palestinian demonstrators and Israeli soldiers faced off along the fence hemming in the Gaza Strip for a second week on Friday. Nine Palestinians were killed, including two teenagers, and a thousand were wounded, Palestinian officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/07/world/middleeast/07gaza5/merlin_136464318_189ab8b6-7646-4ea1-9e9c-f688820cf9af-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/07/world/middleeast/07gaza5/merlin_136464318_189ab8b6-7646-4ea1-9e9c-f688820cf9af-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/07/world/middleeast/07gaza5/merlin_136464318_189ab8b6-7646-4ea1-9e9c-f688820cf9af-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/07/world/middleeast/07gaza5/merlin_136464318_189ab8b6-7646-4ea1-9e9c-f688820cf9af-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1321, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/07/world/middleeast/07gaza5/07gaza5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/07/world/middleeast/07gaza5/07gaza5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/07/world/middleeast/07gaza5/07gaza5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nine Killed in Gaza as Palestinian Protesters Face Off With Israeli Soldiers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '10 Killed and 1,000 Wounded in Protest at Gaza Fence, Palestinians Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Border Barriers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Khan Younis (Gaza Strip)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'vis-photo', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-06T13:08:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Halbfinger, Iyad Abuheweila and Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee667974-583b-5243-a3fc-6b754bbc00f0', 'word_count': 1282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee667974-583b-5243-a3fc-6b754bbc00f0'}, {'abstract': 'The basic story of a strong labor market remains intact, but a disappointing report is a sign that the U.S. is not in some extraordinary boom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/06/upshot/the-march-jobs-numbers-show-the-economy-is-sound-but-far-from-invincible.html', 'snippet': 'The basic story of a strong labor market remains intact, but a disappointing report is a sign that the U.S. is not in some extraordinary boom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The March employment numbers were a disappointment, but only relative to extremely optimistic expectations. The basic story of a robust United States job market remains very much intact — though with an important asterisk.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/07/upshot/07up-jobs/merlin_136291437_1a6b3d15-568d-4159-bd78-fc33eb205a41-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/07/upshot/07up-jobs/merlin_136291437_1a6b3d15-568d-4159-bd78-fc33eb205a41-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/07/upshot/07up-jobs/merlin_136291437_1a6b3d15-568d-4159-bd78-fc33eb205a41-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/07/upshot/07up-jobs/merlin_136291437_1a6b3d15-568d-4159-bd78-fc33eb205a41-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/07/upshot/07up-jobs/07up-jobs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75,