8f6231-1f2e-5c06-b9b9-b0fb2b541f2b', 'word_count': 1107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/638f6231-1f2e-5c06-b9b9-b0fb2b541f2b'}, {'abstract': 'Fill the days ahead with some mighty meals: gyros with oven fries, pasta with fried lemons and a buttermilk roast chicken.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/08/dining/what-to-cook-this-week-newsletter.html', 'snippet': 'Fill the days ahead with some mighty meals: gyros with oven fries, pasta with fried lemons and a buttermilk roast chicken.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. This might have been a great afternoon to make a deep-dish apple pie, pull the last of the good apples out of the refrigerator or the big tub down in the chilly basement, slice them and pile them high and bake them in buttery crusts so there’s something warm and fragrant to eat after dinner: fried chicken, for instance, with biscuits and pickleback slaw.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/08mag-ondessert1-copy/08mag-08ondessert-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/08mag-ondessert1-copy/08mag-08ondessert-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/08mag-ondessert1-copy/08mag-08ondessert-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/08mag-ondessert1-copy/08mag-08ondessert-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/08mag-ondessert1-copy/08mag-ondessert1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/08mag-ondessert1-copy/08mag-ondessert1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/08mag-ondessert1-copy/08mag-ondessert1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Cook This Week', 'kicker': 'What to Cook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-08T14:30:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36529630-930d-5f8d-a1af-ec9fee37161b', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36529630-930d-5f8d-a1af-ec9fee37161b'}, {'abstract': 'Don Graham’s new book tells the story of how the epic starring James Dean and Elizabeth Taylor was made.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/08/books/giant-don-graham-interview.html', 'snippet': 'Don Graham’s new book tells the story of how the epic starring James Dean and Elizabeth Taylor was made.', 'lead_paragraph': '“In Texas, as ‘Giant’ so brilliantly points out, big is always better than small; and if the only way to be big is to lose big, then well, so be it,” Larry McMurtry wrote in The New York Times in 1996. The director George Stevens’s film, starring Elizabeth Taylor and James Dean, and based on Edna Ferber’s 1952 novel of the same name, was released in 1956. It earned Stevens an Oscar and was nominated in several other categories, including Best Picture. (It lost to “Around the World in 80 Days.”) Don Graham’s new book tells the story of how this epic about the ranching life, the oil business, clashing cultures and the changing fortunes of generations made it to the screen. Below, Mr. Graham, an English professor at the University of Texas at Austin, discusses how his students’ reaction to the movie helped inspire the book, how Stevens’s experiences during World War II influenced the film and more.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/09/books/09graham-five3/09graham-five3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/09/books/09graham-five3/09graham-five3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/09/books/09graham-five3/09graham-five3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/09/books/09graham-five3/09graham-five3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1401, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/09/books/09graham-five3/09graham-five3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/09/books/09graham-five3/09graham-five3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/09/books/09graham-five3/09graham-five3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tell Us 5 Things About Your Book: Bringing ‘Giant’ to the Big Screen', 'kicker': 'Q. & A.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Telling a ‘Giant’ Tale  Big Enough for Texas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Don B', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Giant (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Giant: Elizabeth Taylor, Rock Hudson, James Dean, Edna Ferber, and the Making of a Legendary American Film (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-08T15:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/0623c075-32bb-5c61-bffb-5434563fbbc9', 'word_count': 984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0623c075-32bb-5c61-bffb-5434563fbbc9'}, {'abstract': 'Six months after Mattek-Sands’s horrific knee injury at Wimbledon, Justin Sands had a similar incident while hiking, and he joined her in the gym for recovery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/08/sports/tennis/bethanie-mattek-sands-knee.html', 'snippet': 'Six months after Mattek-Sands’s horrific knee injury at Wimbledon, Justin Sand