'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexuals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-09T09:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathaniel Frank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c393942-a924-54bf-8cc7-31dd1fddb25c', 'word_count': 883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c393942-a924-54bf-8cc7-31dd1fddb25c'}, {'abstract': 'Income-driven repayment is one of the government’s least well-known, most progressive programs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/09/opinion/student-loan-reform-prosper-act.html', 'snippet': 'Income-driven repayment is one of the government’s least well-known, most progressive programs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the most important — but least known — achievements of the Obama administration was the expansion of the income-driven repayment program for federal student loans. The program aims to make student loan payments affordable for everyone, regardless of their income. But Republicans, in their endless quest to undo everything Mr. Obama did, are now trying to dismantle the program under the guise of reform, citing misleading claims of high costs and low effectiveness. In fact, the program’s costs are low, and the student loan system as a whole is financially self-sustaining. More important, we should be increasing investment in higher education and support for students, not the reverse.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/09/opinion/09Brooks/merlin_128313353_8ce2db71-542f-4af9-a26a-1c7346a19485-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/09/opinion/09Brooks/merlin_128313353_8ce2db71-542f-4af9-a26a-1c7346a19485-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/09/opinion/09Brooks/merlin_128313353_8ce2db71-542f-4af9-a26a-1c7346a19485-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/09/opinion/09Brooks/merlin_128313353_8ce2db71-542f-4af9-a26a-1c7346a19485-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/09/opinion/09Brooks/09Brooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/09/opinion/09Brooks/09Brooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/09/opinion/09Brooks/09Brooks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Let the G.O.P. Dismantle Obama’s Student Loan Reforms', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pell Grants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-09T09:45:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By John R. Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5128f156-6e2b-55ea-8bcc-356b38c944dc', 'word_count': 963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5128f156-6e2b-55ea-8bcc-356b38c944dc'}, {'abstract': 'The celebrated designer first made his name four decades ago, in Manhattan. Here, he shares some of his many inspirations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/09/t-magazine/michael-kors-80s-photos-inspiration.html', 'snippet': 'The celebrated designer first made his name four decades ago, in Manhattan. Here, he shares some of his many inspirations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Growing up in Merrick, Long Island, Michael Kors was surrounded by women who loved fashion: “My mother was a former Revlon model, my grandmother was obsessed with Bill Blass and beige and I had two midriff-bearing aunts who idolized Cher,” says the designer, who drew dresses in the sand at the family beach club, where he first observed the leisure-class glamour that would become his eponymous label’s signature. “Everyone would arrive to their cabanas wearing bikinis and leave for dinner in evening gowns,” Kors recalls. After high school, he attended the Fashion Institute of Technology in Manhattan, but dropped out after two semesters to work as a window dresser and “sales boy” at Lothar’s clothing boutique on Fifth Avenue (a favorite of Jacqueline Kennedy Onassis and Diana Ross) where he also began selling pieces — crisply tailored blazers, sporty sheaths and maxi skirts — of his own design.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '96', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-kors-slide-ZTLO/05tmag-kors-slide-ZTLO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 487, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-kors-slide-ZTLO/05tmag-kors-slide-ZTLO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 487}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-kors-slide-ZTLO/05tmag-kors-slide-ZTLO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 789, 'width': 973, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-kors-slide-ZTLO/05tmag-kors-slide-ZTLO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 789, 'width': 973, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-kors-slide-ZTLO/05tmag-kors-slide-ZTLO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-kors-slide-ZTLO/05tmag-kors-slide-ZTLO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag