d86-519f-9afa-de40879c73eb', 'word_count': 1099, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d60fd1d-fd86-519f-9afa-de40879c73eb'}, {'abstract': 'The penultimate episode of the season was the show’s darkest and best hour to date.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/09/arts/television/here-and-now-recap-dream-logic.html', 'snippet': 'The penultimate episode of the season was the show’s darkest and best hour to date.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Get ready for the future: It is murder,” the prophet Leonard Cohen warned in one of his bleakest songs, “The Future.” That lyric popped into my head midway through this week’s episode of “Here and Now” and lingered there for quite a while afterward. Although it didn’t actually feature any coldblooded killings, the episode, which is the penultimate chapter of Season 1, was the show’s darkest and best hour to date. It was also the first episode in which many of the characters were forced to think seriously about their futures.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/arts/08hereandnow-recap/08hereandnow-recap-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/08/arts/08hereandnow-recap/08hereandnow-recap-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/arts/08hereandnow-recap/08hereandnow-recap-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/arts/08hereandnow-recap/08hereandnow-recap-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type