tion': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c87aff81-24a0-5fa7-884b-6ba3932c9c26', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c87aff81-24a0-5fa7-884b-6ba3932c9c26'}, {'abstract': 'Sfoglini, the Brooklyn-based pasta maker, is selling deeply ridged radiatore for a limited time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/09/dining/radiatore-pasta-sfoglini.html', 'snippet': 'Sfoglini, the Brooklyn-based pasta maker, is selling deeply ridged radiatore for a limited time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As spring ramps up (pun intended), Sfoglini, the Brooklyn-based maker of unusual organic pastas, is selling deeply ridged radiator pasta (in Italian, radiatore) seasoned with nettles. The wild herb gives the camouflage-green pasta a grassy flavor, making it a fine partner for a light, creamy sauce. Thin some Greek yogurt with pasta water, and toss it with the pasta, adding olive oil and shavings of ricotta salata. It’s sold until the end of May. And in a month, yes, Sfoglini will have ramp fusilli: Nettle Radiators, $7.99 for one pound, sfoglini.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11BURNERPASTA/11BURNERPASTA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11BURNERPASTA/11BURNERPASTA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11BURNERPASTA/11BURNERPASTA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11BURNERPASTA/11BURNERPASTA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'widt