aph': 'Minna Kao’s work as a fashion designer has led her to the kitchen. She designs and sells aprons and uniforms to restaurants, and makes some of her aprons to be used at home. Her products are made with sustainable fabrics and without toxic dyes. The simple, adjustable, unisex designs have handy pockets. Aprons, $78 to $114, boworkwear.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burneraprons-1522852218539/11burneraprons-1522852218539-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burneraprons-1522852218539/11burneraprons-1522852218539-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burneraprons-1522852218539/11burneraprons-1522852218539-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burneraprons-1522852218539/11burneraprons-1522852218539-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burneraprons-1522852218539/11burneraprons-1522852218539-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burneraprons-1522852218539/11burneraprons-1522852218539-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burneraprons-1522852218539/11burneraprons-1522852218539-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fashion Designer Looks to the Kitchen', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Protect: Designer’s Taste Turns To Kitchen for Inspiration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kao, Minna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-09T17:11:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3a8440a-b0be-5619-80f9-934d05634d1d', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3a8440a-b0be-5619-80f9-934d05634d1d'}, {'abstract': 'At his new OddFellows location, Sam Mason said, “it was time to bring them together.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/09/dining/ice-cream-coffee-oddfellows.html', 'snippet': 'At his new OddFellows location, Sam Mason said, “it was time to bring them together.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'An OddFellows Ice Cream outlet with a very particular focus — coffee and cream — is opening Wednesday. An assortment of drinks and confections featuring the combination of ice cream and coffee will be dispensed at the counter in the bright corner shop with swimming pool turquoise banquettes, where they will also serve the two elements independently. “I thought it was time to bring them together,” said Sam Mason, who owns OddFellows with Mohan Kumar. Andy Mullins is the coffee geek who figures out which coffees to serve and with what. Espresso with whipped cream (con panna) in flavors like saffron, riffs on affogato, cold-brew milkshakes, artfully layered café liégeois, and coffee soft serve are on the menu. Du’s Donuts provide something to nibble: Coffee & Cream by OddFellows Ice Cream Co., 55 East Houston Street (Mott Street), oddfellowsnyc.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burnercoffeencream/11burnercoffeencream-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burnercoffeencream/11burnercoffeencream-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burnercoffeencream/11burnercoffeencream-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burnercoffeencream/11burnercoffeencream-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burnercoffeencream/11burnercoffeencream-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burnercoffeencream/11burnercoffeencream-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burnercoffeencream/11burnercoffeencream-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Natural Combo: Ice Cream and Coffee', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Scream: Coffee Meets Cream As in (Yes!) Ice Cream', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice Cream and Frozen Desserts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'OddFellows Ice Cream Co (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffeehouses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mason, Sam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-09T17:12:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8b38cfe-25e3-56f2-8d76-fb51334f8d05', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8b38cfe-25e3-56f2-8d76-fb51334f8d05'}, {'abstract': 'The Japanese restaurant Wokuni has opened a fish market at the front of the restaurant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/09/dining/fish-market-wokuni.html', 'snippet': 'The Japanese restaurant Wokuni has opened a fish market at the front of the restaurant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wokuni, a Japanese restaurant that opened last fall, has installed a sakanaya, or fish market, at the front of the restaurant. There, it sells sushi-grade seafood, including bluefin tuna, king yellowtail, and specialties like sea urchin, salmon roe and monkfish liver. The yellowtail and tuna are raised in Japan at the aqua farms owned by Tokyo Ichiban Foods, a large restaurant company that has Wokuni in its lineup. Most of the rest is flown in from Tsukiji Market in Tokyo. Some cuts of fish come grill-ready, seasoned with a thick white-miso marinade. Well-seared, the king yellowtail is lush and succulent: Seafood, from $2 to $32 during restaurant hours, Sakanaya at Wokuni, 327 Lexington Avenue (39th Street), 212-447-1212, wokuninyc.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burnerfish2/11burnerfish2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burnerfish2/11burnerfish2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burnerfish2/11burnerfish2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burnerfish2/11burnerfish2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burnerfish2/11burnerfish2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burnerfish2/11burnerfish2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/dining/11burnerfish2/11burnerfish2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sushi-Grade Fish Straight From Japan', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Shop: Sushi-Grade Seafood Straight From Japan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sushi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japanese Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wokuni (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tokyo Ichiban Foods Co Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-09T17:20:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac3b8d5c-cca6-5d3f-9283-de618f7e5fd5', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac3b8d5c-cca6-5d3f-9283-de618f7e5fd5'}, {'abstract': 'Rawsome Treats, which started selling its raw cakes and confections online five years ago, now has a shop and cafe on the Lower East Side.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/09/dining/rawsome-treats-vegan.html', 'snippet': 'Rawsome Treats, which started selling its raw cakes and confections online five years ago, now has a shop and cafe on the Lower East Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s plenty of deliciousness in the array of bright, layered tarts, cakes and bite-size confections from Watt Sriboonruang, the chef who founded Rawsome Treats about five years ago. She started selling them retail and wholesale online and has just opened her first shop and cafe. She’s a kickboxer from Thailand who says she relies on raw food for energy that does not come with weight gain. Many of her rich, stunning items rely on nuts and nut milks: Rawsome Treats, 158 Orchard Str