ne': {'main': 'Poem: Photo of a Book Burning, Warsaw Indiana', 'kicker': 'Poem', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Photo of a Book Burning, Warsaw Indiana', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-11T09:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Wojahn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wojahn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64f4e165-13c8-51e6-8c71-ff03577f5992', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64f4e165-13c8-51e6-8c71-ff03577f5992'}, {'abstract': 'What’s happening behind the scenes at the sites and apps you know and love and hate, along with a couple that may not be on your radar (or phone). ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/11/style/match-shaadi-league-farmersonly-dating-apps.html', 'snippet': 'What’s happening behind the scenes at the sites and apps you know and love and hate, along with a couple that may not be on your radar (or phone). ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Different studies offer varying assessments of how many people use dating sites and apps, but what we can say with certainty is: a lot. In Match.com’s annual Singles in America Survey, which polls more than 5,000 people who are not Match users, the company found that the No. 1 place where singles meet is online. In 2016, Pew reported that 27 percent of people aged 18 to 24 had used a dating app or site. In 2013, it was 10 percent. The proportion of 55- to 64-year-olds in the same category doubled. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': No