web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/11/travel/five-places-to-go-in-bangkok-ari.html', 'snippet': 'Bangkok’s Ari neighborhood is increasingly a thicket of sleek high-rise buildings and indie cool-kid hangouts radiating international flavors. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Bangkok’s Ari neighborhood could write its own autobiography, it might be called “From Bureaucrats to Baristas.” For decades, the low-lying leafy district was known mainly for its federal ministries, municipal administration offices and gated quasi-suburban homes. Increasingly, however, Ari is a thicket of sleek high-rise buildings and indie cool-kid hangouts with international flavors: German beer gardens, Latin American restaurants, Korean canteens, Japanese izakayas, American-style food trucks and numerous freshly minted cafes stocked with Italian espresso makers. All that’s missing is the crowds. Even on weekends, Ari’s hot spots have free seats and ample breathing room — a rarity in bustling Bangkok.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/travel/15bangkok-5places4/15bangkok-5places4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/15/travel/15bangkok-5places4/15bangkok-5places4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/travel/15bangkok-5places4/15bangkok-5places4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/travel/15bangkok-5places4/15bangkok-5places4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}