'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice Hines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c55c3fe-5664-5b32-b5e4-8675230afe0a', 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c55c3fe-5664-5b32-b5e4-8675230afe0a'}, {'abstract': 'For this issue, the crisis of black infant and maternal mortality in America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/11/magazine/behind-the-cover-4-15-18.html', 'snippet': 'For this issue, the crisis of black infant and maternal mortality in America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kathy Ryan, director of photography: “LaToya Ruby Frazier, renowned for her work documenting her own family as well as families in Flint, Mich., chose to portray Simone Landrum cradling her son Kingston because she wanted to convey the feeling of protectiveness felt by the mother of a black boy born in these turbulent times. We decided that nothing could convey more powerfully the critical issues of black infant and maternal mortality in America than this tender portrait of a child in his first day of life.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/magazine/15mag-cover-bg/15mag-cover-bg-articleLarge-v8.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/15/magazine/15mag-cover-bg/15mag-cover-bg-articleLarge-v8.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/magazine/15mag-cover-bg/15mag-cover-bg-jumbo-v8.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'cap