y that is “comfortable, down to earth.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rinku Thomas thought she loved the elementary school in Hicksville, on Long Island, where she was living temporarily. Then she and her husband, Ashby, moved with their three children to Syosset. Their daughter’s third-grade teacher called out of the blue to report on the girl’s progress. “I never had that before,” Ms. Thomas said. Their son was inspired to read a book every day and write a report about it. He is in kindergarten.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/realestate/15LIVING-SYOSSET-slide-SI5I/15LIVING-SYOSSET-slide-SI5I-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/15/realestate/15LIVING-SYOSSET-slide-SI5I/15LIVING-SYOSSET-slide-SI5I-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/realestate/15LIVING-SYOSSET-slide-SI5I/15LIVING-SYOSSET-slide-SI5I-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/realestate/15LIVING-SYOSSET-slide-SI5I/15LIVING-SYOSSET-slide-SI5I-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/realestate/15LIVING-SYOSSET-slide-SI5I/15LIVING-SYOSSET-slide-SI5I-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/15/realestate/15LIVING-SYOSSET-slide-SI5I/15LIVING-SYOSSET-slide-SI5I-thumbStandar