 way of looking at today’s biggest policy dilemmas might help heal partisan divisions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/11/opinion/localism-partisanship-local-politics.html', 'snippet': 'A community-based way of looking at today’s biggest policy dilemmas might help heal partisan divisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I live in one of those old towns that was not built for cars. Its Main Street is narrow, hedged in with historic stone houses and walls. As commuter traffic has intensified over the past several years, it’s become increasingly dangerous to walk along Main Street.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/opinion/11olmstead/11olmstead-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/11/opinion/11olmstead/11olmstead-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/opinion/11olmstead/11olmstead-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/opinion/11olmstead/11olmstead-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/opinion/11olmstead/11olmstead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/11/opinion/11olmstead/11olmstead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/11/opinion/11olmstead/11olmstead-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can ‘Localism’ Restore Sanity to U.S. Politics?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Local Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brookings Institution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berry, Wendell', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Jane', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-11T14:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gracy Olmstead', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gracy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olmstead', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6eb44b86-bee0-5636-a653-e0f0144b80fe', 'word_count': 1215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6eb44b86-bee0-5636-a653-e0f0144b80fe'}, {'abstract': 'Head out to the grill and make some chicken thighs with spicy cashews, or stay indoors with a spring ramen bowl.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/11/dining/what-to-cook-right-now-newsletter.html', 'snippet': 'Head out to the grill and make some chicken thighs with spicy cashews, or stay indoors with a spring ramen bowl.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. The oven stopped working the other day and in the morning I tore the stove apart to figure out why: a burned-out ignitor, $21.16 from the shop on the internet, delivery expected tomorrow. It should take about 20 minutes to install and put everything back together if Mr. Murphy doesn’t poke his head into the proceedings and set me on fire. Meantime, there’s been a toaster oven and rusting patio grill to explore.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/14/dining/24GRILLS4/14GRILLS4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/06/14/dining/24GRILLS4/14GRILLS4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/14/dining/24GRILLS4/14GRILLS4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/14/dining/24GRILLS4/14GRILLS4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1463, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/14/dining/24GRILLS4/14GRILLS4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/06/14/dining/24GRILLS4/14GRILLS4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/06/14/dining/24GRILLS4/14GRILLS4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Cook Right Now', 'kicker': 'What to Cook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-11T14:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fab37b99-1f81-50e8-bc9c-afe933a43aa5', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fab37b99-1f81-50e8-bc9c-afe933a43aa5'}, {'abstract': 'David Wojnarowicz saved an assortment of masks, rubber Frankenstein gloves and a pair of droopy-eyed glasses — all cataloged after his death in 1992.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/11/t-magazine/art/david-wojnarowicz-halloween.html', 'snippet': 'David Wojnarowicz saved an assortment of masks, rubber Frankenstein gloves and a pair of droopy-eyed glasses — all cataloged after his death in 1992.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a teenager on the streets in the early 1970s, artist David Wojnarowicz frequented the then-seedy blocks around Times Square, hustling among junkies, drug dealers and pimps. The harsh reality of his New York City childhood would later become paramount to his work — black-and-white photography, Super 8 films, paintings — stripping away the layers of civil society to reveal modern culture in all its raw brutality: the hypocrisy of government and religion, the marginalization gay people faced during the Reagan era. But his personal artifacts, many of which are now archived at N.Y.U.’s Fales Library & Special Collections along with his work, reveal Wojnarowicz’s humorous side, including an assembly of Halloween ornaments and decorations cataloged after his death in 1992. “He had over 400 objects in the collection,” says Marvin J. Taylor, the director of Fales. “He managed to hold on to everything despite moving around a lot throughout his life.” A retrospective of Wojnarowicz’s work opens July 13 at the Whitney Museum of American Art. ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '134', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-halloween-slide-2R3I/05tmag-halloween-slide-2R3I-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-halloween-slide-2R3I/05tmag-halloween-slide-2R3I-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-halloween-slide-2R3I/05tmag-halloween-slide-2R3I-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-halloween-slide-2R3I/05tmag-halloween-slide-2R3I-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-halloween-slide-2R3I/05tmag-halloween-slide-2R3I-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-halloween-slide-2R3I/05tmag-halloween-slide-2R3I-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-halloween-slide-2R3I/05tmag-halloween-slide-2R3I-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Artist’s Halloween Paraphernalia, Illustrated', 