, 'snippet': 'Before a win over the Marlins, the Mets learned of their first big injury of the season: a torn ligament in the throwing arm of catcher Travis d’Arnaud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — Only two weeks old, the Mets’ 2018 season already has a distinctly different feel from last year’s campaign. After yet another comeback, a 4-1 victory over the Miami Marlins on Wednesday for their eighth consecutive win, the Mets extended their franchise-best start to 10-1. With Zack Wheeler’s stellar start, the Mets’ oft-injured Big Five starters finally made one mostly ceremonial turn through the rotation.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/12/sports/12metsweb/merlin_136723164_3abed3b4-65ed-4b49-ac07-afdbee08e498-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/12/sports/12metsweb/merlin_136723164_3abed3b4-65ed-4b49-ac07-afdbee08e498-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/12/sports/12metsweb/merlin_136723164_3abed3b4-65ed-4b49-ac07-afdbee08e498-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/12/sports/12metsweb/merlin_136723164_3abed3b4-65ed-4b49-ac07-afdbee08e498-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/12/sports/12metsweb/12metsweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2