ew-bel-powley.html', 'snippet': 'Fritz Böhm’s creature feature is functional but lacks flavor, our critic writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Wildling,” Anna (played at high school age by Bel Powley), can be excused for not recognizing that her life is a checklist of horror movie tropes. After all, she was raised in captivity by a man she calls Daddy (Brad Dourif), who kept her confined and incurious with an elaborate set of myths and rules. He even gave her injections to stunt her puberty.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/13/arts/13wildling/merlin_136486059_ab8f66be-4355-44cb-93fc-2529f1b56d6e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/13/arts/13wildling/merlin_136486059_ab8f66be-4355-44cb-93fc-2529f1b56d6e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/13/arts/13wildling/merlin_136486059_ab8f66be-4355-44cb-93fc-2529f1b56d6e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/13/arts/13wildling/merlin_136486059_ab8f66be-4355-44cb-93fc-2529f1b56d6e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/13/arts/13wildling/merlin_136486059_ab8f66be-4355-44cb-93fc-2529f1b56d6e-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/13/arts/13wildling/merlin_136486059_ab8f66be-4355-44cb-93fc-2529f1b56d