t the world doesn’t always spare children. The students of Parkland, Fla., know this well. In my daughters’ school, children are mourning a beloved first grader who died from complications of the flu. Her friends are 5, 6, 7 — too young to face such grief, we think helplessly, except that suddenly they must.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/books/review/15KIDS1/15KIDS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 826, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/15/books/review/15KIDS1/15KIDS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 826}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/books/review/15KIDS1/15KIDS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 744, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/books/review/15KIDS1/15KIDS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1453, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/books/review/15KIDS1/15KIDS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/15/books/review/15KIDS1/15KIDS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/books/review/15KIDS1/15KIDS1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Going Gets Tough, These Kids Find Their Way', 'kicker': 'Chil