is his new one, a prequel called “Rebound.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'SLAM DUNK: “I believe that books are like amusement parks and sometimes kids ought to be able to choose the ride that’s going to thrill them,” the children’s book author Kwame Alexander says. His last novel — “The Crossover,” a Newbery-winning, hip-hop-inflected tale of basketball-loving twin boys Josh and Jordan — was written in verse, as is his new one, a prequel called “Rebound.” It enters the middle-grade hardcover list at No. 3.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/books/review/22-BKS-LIST/22-BKS-LIST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 548, 'width': 587, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/books/review/22-BKS-LIST/22-BKS-LIST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 548, 'width': 587, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/books/review/22-BKS-LIST/22-BKS-LIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/22/books/review/22-BKS-LIST/22-BKS-LIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/books/review/22-BKS-LIST/22-BKS-LIST-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Turning Basketball Lovers Into Book Lovers, a Stanza at a Time', 'kicker': 'Inside the List', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'v