de, but it would be a grave political mistake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Trump this week claimed the power to fire the special counsel, Robert Mueller, “directly.” In response, the Senate Judiciary Committee seems poised to prohibit Mr. Mueller’s removal by the president except “for cause,” which generally requires a crime, violation of the law, or abuse of power. While the Senate has the politics right, Mr. Trump has the Constitution on his side.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/13/opinion/13Yoo/merlin_122210810_8ae9bf08-511c-40a5-a189-ad0f2baf0376-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/13/opinion/13Yoo/merlin_122210810_8ae9bf08-511c-40a5-a189-ad0f2baf0376-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/13/opinion/13Yoo/merlin_122210810_8ae9bf08-511c-40a5-a189-ad0f2baf0376-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/13/opinion/13Yoo/merlin_122210810_8ae9bf08-511c-40a5-a189-ad0f2baf0376-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/13/opinion/13Yoo/13Yoo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/13/opinion/13Yoo/13Yoo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/13/op