iter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/115f5039-9e76-5a29-ad96-11f03c074210', 'word_count': 1077, 'uri': 'nyt://article/115f5039-9e76-5a29-ad96-11f03c074210'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Lubovitch, who’s been a choreographer for 50 years, talks about his work and learning from the best: Graham, Limón and the stage of a nightclub.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/13/arts/lar-lubovitch-50th-anniversary-joyce.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Lubovitch, who’s been a choreographer for 50 years, talks about his work and learning from the best: Graham, Limón and the stage of a nightclub.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The choreographer Lar Lubovitch didn’t discover dance until college, where he had gone in hopes of becoming a painter. The impulse to fill a canvas hasn’t left him. When he describes making a dance, he does so not only in kinetic terms but through the prism of painting: “I’m reacting to the effect the music has on me and making that visual by painting the space and the time that the music is occupying,” he said recently over lunch at a cafe near his Chelsea apartment', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/arts/15LARLUBOVITCH1/merlin_136021956_ca22be69-a015-45a8-aa4e-77353c317d9d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/15/arts/15LARLUBOVITCH1/merlin_136021956_ca22be69-a015-45a8-aa4e-77353c317d9d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/arts/15LARLUBOVITCH1/merlin_136021956_ca22be69-a015-45a8-aa4e-77353c317d9d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', '