1af7358'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Comey, the former F.B.I. director fired by President Trump in 2017, appeared in an hourlong interview on ABC Sunday night. Here is some of what he had to say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/15/us/politics/comey-abc-interview-excerpts.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Comey, the former F.B.I. director fired by President Trump in 2017, appeared in an hourlong interview on ABC Sunday night. Here is some of what he had to say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABC News aired an hourlong interview on Sunday with James B. Comey, the F.B.I. director fired by President Trump last year. George Stephanopoulos, ABC’s chief anchor, interviewed Mr. Comey, who is promoting his new book, “A Higher Loyalty,” for five hours in all. ABC published a complete transcript of their conversation. Here are highlights and analysis from that transcript.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/14/us/politics/excerpts-comey-1/excerpts-comey-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 791, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/14/us/politics/excerpts-comey-1/excerpts-comey-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 791}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/14/us/politics/excerpts-comey-1/excerpts-comey-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 778, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/14/us/politics/excerpts-comey-1/excerpts-comey-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1555, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/14/us/politics/excerpts-comey-1/excerpts-comey-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/14/us/politics/excerpts-comey-1/excerpts-comey-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/14/us/politics/excerpts-comey-1/excerpts-comey-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'James Comey’s Interview on ABC’s ‘20/20’: Annotated Excerpts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': ' Notable Moments In ABC’s Interview  With Ex-F.B.I. Chief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Comey, James B', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC News', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-16T01:48:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21966473-087b-5bb6-8753-c52b60e0c216', 'word_count': 3743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21966473-087b-5bb6-8753-c52b60e0c216'}, {'abstract': 'The father-son relationship between Charles and Chuck was already on the rocks. This week, it took a turn for the disturbing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/15/arts/television/billions-recap-hell-of-a-ride.html', 'snippet': 'The father-son relationship between Charles and Chuck was already on the rocks. This week, it took a turn for the disturbing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chuck Rhoades Jr. and Charles Rhoades Sr. are at war. They have been since the last season of “Billions,” when son betrayed father as part of a plot by Chuck to ruin his nemesis, Bobby Axelrod. But the most powerful weapon wielded in the conflict so far hasn’t been a legal threat or a stock swindle. It’s the kiss that Charles plants square on Chuck’s mouth, hands locked on his son’s head to prevent him from pulling away.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/arts/15billions-recap/15billions-recap-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/15/arts/15billions-recap/15billions-recap-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/arts/15billions-recap/15billions-recap-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/arts/15billions-recap/15billions-recap-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1537, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/arts/15billions-recap/15billions-recap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/15/arts/15billions-recap/15billions-recap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/15/arts/15billions-recap/15billions-recap-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Billions’ Season 3, Episode 4 Recap: Sealed With a Kiss', 'kicker': 'Billions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Billions (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-16T03:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sean T. Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sean', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0dfe1500-b210-522c-a84c-c6c5b79d1017', 'word_count': 1275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dfe1500-b210-522c-a84c-c6c5b79d1017'}, {'abstract': 'Everyone but Gail seems exceptionally calm about Paul’s kidnapping, even after new and worrying details emerge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/15/arts/television/trust-recap-thats-all-folks.html', 'snippet': 'Everyone but Gail seems exceptionally calm about Paul’s kidnapping, even after new and worrying details emerge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Italians historically know a lot about kidnappings. Between 1970 and 1990, more than 600 of them were recorded nationally; between 1975 and 1983, the annual average was more than 50. Kidnappings became such common practice in Italy that a systematized protocol formed around them: Mafia or independent bandits from Calabria and Sardinia would target wealthy families in the North and abscond with their victims to the densely-wooded mountains of the south, where they would hide until a ransom was paid. Kidnappers were also known to sell their victims to other criminal groups as a faster means to cash before the original ransom demands were met.', 'source': 'The New York Times