, {'abstract': 'Four female senators, Susan Collins of Maine, Amy Klobuchar of Minnesota, Heidi Heitkamp of North Dakota, and Joni Ernst of Iowa, chat at a TimesTalk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/16/us/politics/collins-ernst-klobuchar-heitkamp.html', 'snippet': 'Four female senators, Susan Collins of Maine, Amy Klobuchar of Minnesota, Heidi Heitkamp of North Dakota, and Joni Ernst of Iowa, chat at a TimesTalk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — It has been 86 years since Hattie Wyatt Caraway of Arkansas became the first woman elected to the United States Senate, and women remain woefully underrepresented in the chamber. Women make up nearly 51 percent of the United States population but just 23 percent of the Senate, an all-time high, nonetheless, after Cindy Hyde-Smith was sworn in as the new senator from Mississippi this month .', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/16/us/16DC-TIMESTALK/16DC-TIMESTALK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/16/us/16DC-TIMESTALK/16DC-TIMESTALK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/16/us/16DC-TIMESTALK/16DC-TIMESTALK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/16/us/16DC-TIMESTALK/16DC-TIMESTALK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/16/us/16DC-TIMESTALK/16DC-TIMESTALK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 