4abdf5-ecd1-5d98-91ca-8e981e2d7c8e'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time, an entry from France, Esquirrou, was the grand-prize winner at the World Cheese Championships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/16/dining/world-cheese-championship-esquirrou.html', 'snippet': 'For the first time, an entry from France, Esquirrou, was the grand-prize winner at the World Cheese Championships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the World Cheese Championships held last month in Madison, Wis., the grand prize winner was Esquirrou, a sheep-milk cheese from France’s Basque region. Despite the hundreds of cheeses produced in France, it was the first time a French cheese had been crowned. There were 3,402 cheeses in the competition. The cheese, made from the unpasteurized milk of black and red-faced sheep and aged for six months, has a pale amber rind and delivers a toasty brioche scent with herbaceous notes. Its texture is smooth, on the firm side; it has a lingering, nutty flavor; and it melts beautifully: $32 a pound at Dean & DeLuca stores in New York.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/dining/18burnercheese/18burnercheese-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/18/dining/18burnercheese/18burnercheese-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/dining/18burnercheese/18burnercheese-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/dining/18burnercheese/18burnercheese-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1155, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_na