t://article/bc55f24e-0348-531a-bf37-e6748f79bb6f'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers from both parties took the prime minister to task over the bombing of Syria, saying she was accountable to them, not the “whims of the U.S. president.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/16/world/europe/theresa-may-uk-parliament-syria-corbyn.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers from both parties took the prime minister to task over the bombing of Syria, saying she was accountable to them, not the “whims of the U.S. president.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — After ordering British forces into action in Syria, Prime Minister Theresa May faced criticism from lawmakers on Monday, with many of them seeming to resent being bypassed over the decision, more than the strikes themselves.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theresa May Earns Cold Reception in U.K. Parliament Over Syria Attacks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cold Reception for May in Parliament', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conservative Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labour Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blair, Tony', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'May, Theresa M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corbyn, Jeremy (1949- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-16T20:33:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename':