: 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chappatte', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b6957a1-f0f1-5765-8ccc-cd0e3f9a6812', 'word_count': 3, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b6957a1-f0f1-5765-8ccc-cd0e3f9a6812'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Jones and his conspiracy theory website Infowars have long claimed that the killing of 26 people at the Connecticut elementary school was a “giant hoax.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/17/business/media/alex-jones-sandy-hook.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Jones and his conspiracy theory website Infowars have long claimed that the killing of 26 people at the Connecticut elementary school was a “giant hoax.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three parents whose children were killed at Sandy Hook Elementary School in 2012 filed a defamation lawsuit on Tuesday against Alex Jones, the right-wing conspiracy theorist who has long claimed the shooting was “completely fake” and a “giant hoax” perpetrated by opponents of the Second Amendment.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/us/18xp-infowars2/18xp-infowars2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/18/us/18xp-infowars2/18xp-infowars2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/us/18xp-infowars2/18xp-infowars2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/us/18xp-infowars2/18xp-infowars2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1532, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/us/18xp-infowars2/18xp-infowars2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/18/us/18xp-infowars2/18xp-infowars2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/us/18xp-infowars2/18xp-infowars2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sandy Hook Parents Sue Alex Jones for Defamation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sandy Hook Parents Seek Damages From Conspiracist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Shootings and Armed Attacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Alex (1974- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-17T12:48:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Express', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Haag', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haag', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd0499cf-0285-577b-bbf2-b35fa3e4b3f0', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd0499cf-0285-577b-bbf2-b35fa3e4b3f0'}, {'abstract': 'In the early ’80s, beguiling muses like Patti Hansen, Farida Khelfa and Pat Cleveland were not just faces, but names — and paved the way for ’90s supermodels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/17/t-magazine/muses-1980s-patti-hansen-farida-khelfa.html', 'snippet': 'In the early ’80s, beguiling muses like Patti Hansen, Farida Khelfa and Pat Cleveland were not just faces, but names — and paved the way for ’90s supermodels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the earliest appearances of the muses was in a narrative poem called “Theogony” by the Greek poet Hesiod, who wrote around 700 B.C. that they were nine sisters born of Zeus and his lover Mnemosyne, or memory. Of them he wrote, “they plucked and gave me a rod, a shoot of sturdy laurel, a marvelous thing, and breathed into me a divine voice.” Homer invoked the muse for his epic poem (“Sing to me of the man, Muse”) as did Virgil. Over time, the muse became a less incantatory figure and more of a sexual one: The word is commonly used, for example, as a shorthand for the many wives and lovers Pablo Picasso captured in his work. With the rise of the model as celebrity in the latter half of the 20th century, the muse became more objectified. She could be the woman a fashion designer trusted to wear his clothes, both on and off the runway. Or she could be a figure of whom a world-famous photographer’s lens never tired. These women and their looks — from Misia Sert’s bohemian opulence at the turn of the last century to Twiggy’s sprightly boyishness in the 1960s — can be as much an expression of their times as their era’s music, literature or even politics.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '112', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-group-slide-FJN5/05tmag-group-slide-FJN5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-group-slide-FJN5/05tmag-group-slide-FJN5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-group-slide-FJN5/05tmag-group-slide-FJN5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-group-slide-FJN5/05tmag-group-slide-FJN5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-group-slide-FJN5/05tmag-group-slide-FJN5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-group-slide-FJN5/05tmag-group-slide-FJN5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-group-slide-FJN5/05tmag-group-slide-FJN5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Models Became as Famous as the Artists they Inspired', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Muses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cleveland, Pat (1950- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Eighties', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-17T12:54:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 's