t_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Auster, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Auster, Sophie (1987- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cassavetes, Nick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hustvedt, Siri', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannes International Film Festival', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-17T13:12:51+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barbara Anastacio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barbara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anastacio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/4f9114c8-adf2-599d-ae43-5dbb7dba0988', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/4f9114c8-adf2-599d-ae43-5dbb7dba0988'}, {'abstract': 'Growing up amid grit and glamour, these ’80s kids learned how to make creative lives of their own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/17/t-magazine/new-york-1980s-kids-gaby-hoffmann-zoe-jackson.html', 'snippet': 'Growing up amid grit and glamour, these ’80s kids learned how to make creative lives of their own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you were a child, you likely didn’t watch “Gigi” on the TV in your parents’ townhouse with the Studio 54 impresario Steve Rubell, as New York City’s brightest social and creative lights rang in the new year on the floors below. The novelist Kurt Vonnegut probably didn’t take a liking to you at a social gathering, showing you off to guests as if you were his very own 3-year-old. And it’s virtually certain that even if you did call your own father by his first name, and even if that name happened to be “Don,” your dad was decidedly not the legendary artist Donald Judd, nor did you live in a cast-iron building turned permanent Minimalist art installation in the heart of SoHo, at a time when the neighborhood was not a tony shopping destination but a kind of frontier village — albeit one with loading docks and factories instead of vegetable patches and chicken coops.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '114', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-group-slide-BEO5/05tmag-group-slide-BEO5-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-group-slide-BEO5/05tmag-group-slide-BEO5-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-group-slide-BEO5/05tmag-group-slide-BEO5-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-group-slide-BEO5/05tmag-group-slide-BEO5-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1535, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-group-slide-BEO5/05tmag-group-slide-BEO5-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-group-slide-BEO5/05tmag-group-slide-BEO5-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/05/t-magazine/05tmag-group-slide-BEO5/05tmag-group-slide-BEO5-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Children of New York City’s Greatest Generation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Kids', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Creativity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Eighties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Auster, Sophie (1987- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffmann, Gaby', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richardson Jackson, LaTanya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-17T13:14:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Naomi Fry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Naomi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e48aa3f-27f6-5092-8227-e1025b677c42', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e48aa3f-27f6-5092-8227-e1025b677c42'}, {'abstract': 'If you want a compelling case that, yes, we arriviste New Yorkers may have indeed missed the party, one has only to look to the 36 months between the beginning of 1981 and the end of 1983.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/17/t-magazine/culture-issue-editor-letter.html', 'snippet': 'If you want a compelling case that, yes, we arriviste New Yorkers may have indeed missed the party, one has only to look to the 36 months between the beginning of 1981 and the end of 1983.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One thing that has united every New York transplant, probably since the beginning, is the persistent suspicion that you have arrived just a few months too late, that the circus that drew you to the city pulled up stakes just before you got here. This is certainly true for me: When I was young, my family and I lived in an unfashionable part of the Upper East Side before moving to Baltimore in 1980. A decade later, as a teenager in Honolulu, I would read The Village Voice and listen to Lou Reed and sulk, convinced that my parents had deprived me of the dazzling and bohemian childhood I was certain to have experienced had we remained in Manhattan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/t-magazine/03tmag-edletter2/03tmag-edletter2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/t-magazine/03tmag-edletter2/03tmag-edletter2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 733}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/t-magazine/03tmag-edletter2/03tmag-edletter2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 803, 'width': 657, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/t-magazine/03tmag-edletter2/03tmag-edletter2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 803, 'width': 657, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/t-magazine/03tmag-edletter2/03tmag-edletter2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/t-magazine/03tmag-edletter2/03tmag-edletter2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/t-magazine/03tmag-