er': None, 'print_headline': 'Carl Kasell, Sonorous NPR Newsman Who Took a Comic Turn, Dies at 84', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kasell, Carl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Public Radio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Wait, Wait...Don't Tell Me (Radio Program)", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-17T20:47:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Obituaries', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert D. McFadden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1dc0044-6a6a-5834-9fd9-67cf22cc85ee', 'word_count': 1485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1dc0044-6a6a-5834-9fd9-67cf22cc85ee'}, {'abstract': 'Hundreds of you shared your thoughts about what disorder might be affecting our patient Angel. Let’s keep the conversation going.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/17/magazine/readers-respond-to-our-call-for-help-with-a-diagnosis.html', 'snippet': 'Hundreds of you shared your thoughts about what disorder might be affecting our patient Angel. Let’s keep the conversation going.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, I posted the story of Angel, a 23-year-old woman with devastating daily muscle pain and frequent hospitalizations for rhabdomyolysis, the destruction of muscle fibers, often accompanied by coffee-colored urine. We asked you, the readers of The New York Times, to use your collective knowledge and wisdom to help us come up with possible diagnoses that would help her and her primary care provider find an answer. The response has been gratifying. Hundreds of you filled out answer forms, sharing your thoughts about what Angel might have and what she might do to relieve her symptoms or get a diagnosis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers Respond to Our Call for Help With a Diagnosis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muscles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-17T20:56:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Sanders, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanders', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a245f5a-f3cd-57bd-a820-e2c6823a0e29', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a245f5a-f3cd-57bd-a820-e2c6823a0e29'}, {'abstract': 'John P.A. Greenwood pleaded guilty to disorderly conduct and admitted using a racial slur, but denied the assault that left a black student with a bloody nose.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/17/nyregion/cornell-student-hate-crime-charges-dropped.html', 'snippet': 'John P.A. Greenwood pleaded guilty to disorderly conduct and admitted using a racial slur, but denied the assault that left a black student with a bloody nose.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ITHACA, N.Y. — A prosecutor dropped a hate crime charge on Tuesday against a white Cornell University sophomore who was arrested after a fight that involved an anti-black slur, ending a case that led to protests and soul-searching on the Ivy League campus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cornell Student Admits Using Slur as Hate Crime Charges Are Dropped', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hate Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cornell University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cornell Daily Sun (Newspaper)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ivy League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenwood, John P A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shewit, Solomon', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fischetti, Ronald P', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ithaca (NY)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-17T20:57:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bogel-Burroughs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bogel-Burroughs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/422ecc18-b165-5011-8211-2854c0ce7b41', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/422ecc18-b165-5011-8211-2854c0ce7b41'}, {'abstract': 'At Villa Necchi Campiglio in Milan, we toasted the launch of the Salone del Mobile design week with negronis — and installations by the architect Andrea Tognon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/17/t-magazine/t-magazine-celebrates-salone-del-mobile.html', 'snippet': 'At Villa Necchi Campiglio in Milan, we toasted the launch of the Salone del Mobile design week with negronis — and installations by the architect Andrea Tognon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite the threat of rain in Milan last night, the only thing that got wet at T’s party in celebration of Salone del Mobile was a series of curving polystyrene sculptures that bobbed in the pool of the legendary Villa Necchi Campiglio as guests sipped negronis in the surrounding gardens. The sculptures were studies for massive concrete planters recently stationed outside Milan’s La Rinascente department store by the Italian architect Andrea Tognon. To celebrate T’s Design issue, for which Tognon created a special one-off chair from concrete and fur, editor in chief Hanya Yanagihara invited Tognon to fill the villa inside and out with prototypes and models of his furniture. “We played a little bit with the idea that the Villa Necchi is our design workshop,” he said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/17/t-magazine/entertainment/Salone-slide-9I9L/Salone-slide-9I9L-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/17/t-magazine/entertainment/Salone-slide-9I9L/Salone-slide-9I9L-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/17/t-magazine/entertainment/Salone-slide-9I9L/Salone-slide-9I9L-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/17/t-magazine/entertainment/Salone-slide-9I9L/Salone-slide-9I9L-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/17/t-magazine/entertainment/Salone-slide-9I9L/Salone-slide-9I9L-thumbStand