 20 or 30 seconds, use a tourniquet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/18/magazine/how-to-control-bleeding.html', 'snippet': 'Apply pressure. If the blood flow is heavy after 20 or 30 seconds, use a tourniquet.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Apply pressure where the blood is coming out,” says Christopher B. Colwell, the chief of emergency medicine at Zuckerberg San Francisco General Hospital and Trauma Center. You may need to remove or rip open some of the victim’s clothing to access the injury. “Grab a shirt, a towel, a fabric bag — it doesn’t have to be clean,” Colwell says. Put the cloth over the wound, and push down continuously and forcefully on it with both hands until the bleeding stops.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-tip/22mag-22tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 567, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-tip/22mag-22tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 567}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-tip/22mag-22tip-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 967, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-tip/22mag-22tip-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1934, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-tip/22mag-22tip-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-tip/22mag-22tip-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-tip/22mag-22tip-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Control Bleeding', 'kicker': 'Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Control Bleeding', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-18T09:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malia Wollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34e459d2-1154-5b30-88dc-00068f6dea73', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34e459d2-1154-5b30-88dc-00068f6dea73'}, {'abstract': 'The actress, who plays the ferocious General Okoye in “Black Panther,” says that she “would never even attempt” to Kardashianize her face.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/18/style/danai-gurira-black-panther-beauty.html', 'snippet': 'The actress, who plays the ferocious General Okoye in “Black Panther,” says that she “would never even attempt” to Kardashianize her face.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The actress and playwright Danai Gurira was born in Iowa but grew up in Zimbabwe. That may be an explanation for why, when it comes to beauty, Ms. Gurira, who plays the kick-butt General Okoye in “Black Panther,” finds fun in variety. Now living in New York, Los Angeles and Atlanta, Ms. Gurira, 40, will be reprising Okoye for “Avengers: Infinity War,” out later this month. Find out what beauty staples she’s leaning into lately.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/19/fashion/19SKIN-1/merlin_135746325_2932975b-6d40-4db6-a264-f701d0a10553-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 782, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/19/fashion/19SKIN-1/merlin_135746325_2932975b-6d40-4db6-a264-f701d0a10553-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 782}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/19/fashion/19SKIN-1/merlin_135746325_2932975b-6d40-4db6-a264-f701d0a10553-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 786, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/19/fashion/19SKIN-1/merlin_135746325_2932975b-6d40-4db6-a264-f701d0a10553-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1572, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/19/fashion/19SKIN-1/19SKIN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/19/fashion/19SKIN-1/19SKIN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/19/fashion/19SKIN-1/19SKIN-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Danai Gurira Doesn’t Do Contouring', 'kicker': 'Skin Deep', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Danai Gurira Doesn’t Do Contouring', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 's