Valeriya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Safronova', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3271d85-4863-5b91-ac22-d83c3fed9e4d', 'word_count': 1429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3271d85-4863-5b91-ac22-d83c3fed9e4d'}, {'abstract': 'In your opinion, are there certain genres of music that are overlooked as “serious” or “legitimate” enough to win this prestigious award?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/18/learning/what-musical-piece-would-you-nominate-for-a-pulitzer-prize.html', 'snippet': 'In your opinion, are there certain genres of music that are overlooked as “serious” or “legitimate” enough to win this prestigious award?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year, the Pulitzer Prize for music is awarded “for distinguished musical composition by an American that has had its first performance or recording in the United States during the year.” Take a look at the past winners here. What do you notice about these artists and compositions? What do you wonder?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/arts/music/17kendrick-pulitzer1/merlin_136942104_78981cc6-d0a5-4a1a-a1c3-ba5aa57ee624-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 442, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/18/arts/music/17kendrick-pulitzer1/merlin_136942104_78981cc6-d0a5-4a1a-a1c3-ba5aa57ee624-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 442}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/arts/music/17kendrick-pulitzer1/merlin_136942104_78981cc6-d0a5-4a1a-a1c3-ba5aa57ee624-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/arts/music/17kendrick-pulitzer1/merlin_136942104_78981cc6-d0a5-4a1a-a1c3-ba5aa57ee624-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1508, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/arts/music/17kendrick-pulitzer1/17kendrick-pulitzer1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/18/arts/music/17kendrick-pulitzer1/17kendrick-pulitzer1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/arts/music/17kendrick-pulitzer1/17kendrick-pulitzer1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Musical Piece Would You Nominate for a Pulitzer Prize?', 'kicker': 'Student Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-04-18T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalie Proulx', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Proulx', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c34eb32-ec02-5bf7-b6ca-2dc7270ba078', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c34eb32-ec02-5bf7-b6ca-2dc7270ba078'}, {'abstract': 'This generation’s Doctor Spock popularized the swaddle and simple techniques for soothing infants. Why is he now selling a $1,160 robotic bassinet?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/18/magazine/harvey-karp-baby-mogul.html', 'snippet': 'This generation’s Doctor Spock popularized the swaddle and simple techniques for soothing infants. Why is he now selling a $1,160 robotic bassinet?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harvey Karp, the pediatrician, parenting expert and inventor-slash-entrepreneur, cuts an unimposing figure. Lean and agile, with wispy dark hair, blue-rimmed glasses and a bounce in his step, Karp hugs like the Angeleno he has become and deadpans like the New Yorker he once was. Gray has infiltrated his beard and his eyes are a little hooded, but he still makes for a young 66. He used to dress only in blue button-up shirts with matching sweater vests and bulbous ties in a seemingly self-conscious take on the Nutty Professor, but he has graduated to a darker navy, with slim-fitting jeans, an occasional blazer and a pair of Converse or laceless Vans: his transformation into a hip West Coast chief executive — Prius included — complete.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '40', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-karp1/22mag-22karp-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-karp1/22mag-22karp-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-karp1/22mag-22karp-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-karp1/22mag-22karp-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1261, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-karp1/22mag-karp1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-karp1/22mag-karp1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-karp1/22mag-karp1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Harvey Karp Turned Baby Sleep Into Big Business', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Baby Mogul', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karp, Harvey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cribs (Baby Beds)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Happiest Baby on the Block (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-18T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruth Margalit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Margalit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53f7262a-5f21-5c2c-acae-c20d070dbbaa', 'word_count': 4941, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53f7262a-5f21-5c2c-acae-c20d070dbbaa'}, {'abstract': 'Agriculture could pull carbon out of the air and into the soil — but it would mean a whole new way of thinking about how to tend the land.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/18/magazine/dirt-save-earth-carbon-farming-climate-change.html', 'snippet': 'Agriculture could pull carbon out of the air and into the soil — but it would mean a whole new way of thinking about how to tend the land.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When John Wick and his wife, Peggy Rathmann, bought their ranch in Marin County, Calif., in 1998, it was mostly because they needed more space. Rathmann is an acclaimed children’s book author — “Officer Buckle and Gloria” won a Caldecott Medal in 1996 — and their apartment in San Francisco had become cluttered with her illustrations. They picked out the 540-acre ranch in Nicasio mostly for its large barn, which they planned to remake into a spacious studio. Wick, a former construction foreman — they met when he oversaw a renovation of her bathroom — was eager to tackle the project. He knew the area well, having grown up one town away, in Woodacre, where he had what he describes as a “free-range” childhood: little supervision and lots of biking, rope-swinging and playing in the area’s fields and glens.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-carbon1/22mag-carbon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-carbon1/22mag-carbon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-carbon1/22mag-carbon1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-carbon1/22mag-carbon1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'l