www.nytimes.com/2018/04/18/climate/exxon-climate-lawsuit-colorado.html', 'snippet': 'Local governments in California and New York City have sued oil and gas giants. Now Boulder and two Colorado counties have joined the fight. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until recently, communities suing fossil fuel companies over the costs of climate change have been located on the coasts: cities and counties in California, and New York City. But now, the litigation has jumped inland.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/climate/cli-lawsuits/cli-lawsuits-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/18/climate/cli-lawsuits/cli-lawsuits-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/climate/cli-lawsuits/cli-lawsuits-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/climate/cli-lawsuits/cli-lawsuits-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1340, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/climate/cli-lawsuits/cli-lawsuits-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/18/climate/cli-lawsuits/cli-lawsuits-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/18/climate/cli-lawsuits/cli-lawsuits-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Climate Lawsuits, Once Limited to the Coasts, Jump Inland', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plaintiffs Far From Coast Sue Over Climate Change', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Exxon Mobil Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Suncor Energy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boulder (Colo)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-18T09:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Climate', 'section_name': 'Climate', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b28306ed-1d75-5e01-9415-1d6f6991d5f2', 'word_count': 1084, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b28306ed-1d75-5e01-9415-1d6f6991d5f2'}, {'abstract': 'On facing pages, text and image can be brought into intimate conversation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/18/magazine/the-magic-of-books-where-photography-meets-essays.html', 'snippet': 'On facing pages, text and image can be brought into intimate conversation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Design-wise, the most famous collaboration between a writer and a photographer did not end up looking like much of a collaboration at all. Walker Evans contributed a preface to the 1960 reissue of “Let Us Now Praise Famous Men,” the study of poor tenant farmers in Alabama, originally published in 1941; “Walker” crops up a number of times in James Agee’s text, but a formal separation is maintained between the tenderly austere photographs of families and their homes — printed at the beginning — and the 400 pages of Agee’s highly wrought, much-agonized-over text. This, for Gore Vidal, was no bad thing, because it left Evans’s “austere” photos untainted by what “good-hearted, soft-headed admirers of the Saint James (Agee) version” so loved about the sharecroppers’ gospel.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-onphoto1/22mag-onphoto1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-onphoto1/22mag-onphoto1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-onphoto1/22mag-onphoto1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-onphoto1/22mag-onphoto1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-onphoto1/22mag-onphoto1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-onphoto1/22mag-onphoto1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-onphoto1/22mag-onphoto1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Magic of Books Where Photography Meets Essays', 'kicker': 'On Photography', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Magic of Books Where Photography Meets Essays', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berger, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cole, Teju', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Evans, Walker', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Richard', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winogrand, Garry', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Let Us Now Praise Famous Men (Book)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-18T09:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Dyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3b60aa4-a6ae-5da0-9a11-5d7cbba4a097', 'word_count': 1544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3b60aa4-a6ae-5da0-9a11-5d7cbba4a097'}, {'abstract': 'And was it nothing — or something dangerous to worry about?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/18/magazine/why-wouldt-the-lump-under-the-patients-jaw-go-away.html', 'snippet': 'And was it nothing — or something dangerous to worry about?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 40-year-old man stared into the mirror. Lowering his razor, he lifted his chin to see if the lima-bean-size lump was still visible on the right side of his neck, just under his jawbone. His fingers quickly found the small double-lobed bulge. When he first saw it, while shaving maybe a couple of weeks earlier, it was a little tender. The soreness had gone away, but still, the lump made him nervous. Years ago, a friend had found a lump near her collarbone and ended up dying of cancer. He was due for his yearly physical, so he made an appointment to see his doctor. It was probably nothing — but he wanted to hear it from a professional.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-diagnosis1/22mag-22diagnosis-t_CA1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-diagnosis1/22mag-22diagnosis-t_CA1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-diagnosis1/22mag-22diagnosis-t_CA1-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-diagnosis1/22mag-22diagnosis-t_CA1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1491, 'width': 1491, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/magazine/22mag-diagnosis1/22mag-22diagnosis-t_CA1-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'ima