rganization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/98d63a9a-dd76-573c-b050-40c669643713', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/98d63a9a-dd76-573c-b050-40c669643713'}, {'abstract': 'Amal El-Mohtar looks at new retellings of ancient tales, including a space opera, a futuristic “King Lear,” and an eco-thriller.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/19/books/review/merry-spinster-daniel-mallory-ortberg.html', 'snippet': 'Amal El-Mohtar looks at new retellings of ancient tales, including a space opera, a futuristic “King Lear,” and an eco-thriller.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What does it mean to retell a story? Does it mean dressing up a familiar tale in different clothes? Reading it against its grain? Replacing parts of a story like boards in a ship, until an old story’s shape is built of entirely new wood? This month, I’m looking at recent books that are all retellings of one sort or another.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/books/review/22Otherworldly/merlin_136612458_88ef9673-6cee-45e7-a2ff-5a2010ec83cf-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/22/books/review/22Otherworldly/merlin_136612458_88ef9673-6cee-45e7-a2ff-5a2010ec83cf-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/books/review/22Otherworldly/merlin_136612458_88ef9673-6cee-45e7-a2ff-5a2010ec83cf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/22/books/review/22Otherworldly/merlin_136612458_88ef9673-6cee-45e7-a2ff-5a2010ec83cf-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1188