ce for corruption, a former Supreme Court justice quietly made his debut on the political stage, quite possibly upending the contest.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/21/world/americas/21brazil/merlin_137066403_dc785b35-81fd-4b5e-b1e5-7bf8aec1feb2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/21/world/americas/21brazil/merlin_137066403_dc785b35-81fd-4b5e-b1e5-7bf8aec1feb2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/21/world/americas/21brazil/merlin_137066403_dc785b35-81fd-4b5e-b1e5-7bf8aec1feb2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/21/world/americas/21brazil/merlin_137066403_dc785b35-81fd-4b5e-b1e5-7bf8aec1feb2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1484, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/21/world/americas/21brazil/21brazil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/21/world/americas/21brazil/21brazil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/21/world/americas/21brazil/21brazil-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Janitor to Chief Justice: Could Joaquim Barbosa be Brazil’s Next President?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Retired Judge May Shake Up Brazil’s Presidential Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barbosa, Joaquim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brazilian Socialist Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-20T20:38:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shasta Darlington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shasta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Darlington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6141581-69b8-57c4-bd62-62eb1ceda8a8', 'word_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6141581-69b8-57c4-bd62-62eb1ceda8a8'}, {'abstract': 'A by-no-means-exhaustive list of the things our editors (and a few contributors) find interesting on a given week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/20/t-magazine/chloe-sevigny-lipstick-cristaseya-plates-editors-picks.html', 'snippet': 'A by-no-means-exhaustive list of the things our editors (and a few contributors) find interesting on a given week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British ceramic artist Jude Jelfs — who creates curvaceous porcelain vases with what she describes as “flying boobs” and earthenware jugs with wide-open legs — has always been intrigued by the human figure. During a trip to Florence as a teenager, she had an “aesthetic revelation” when she saw Sandro Botticelli’s masterful representations of fleshy goddesses at the Uffizi Gallery. Over the years, the works of Alberto Giacometti, Pablo Picasso and Henry Moore have also influenced her nude-form vessels; her postural pitcher “Aphrodite” brings to mind Henri Matisse’s 1952 paper cutout “Blue Nude II.” But Jelfs’s work is equally informed by her sense of humor: “When I’m walking down the street,” she says, “I can’t help smiling at the thought that everyone is naked under their clothes.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/20/t-magazine/design/20tmag-jude-01/20tmag-jude-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/20/t-magazine/design/20tmag-jude-01/20tmag-jude-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/20/t-magazine/design/20tmag-jude-01/20tmag-jude-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/20/t-magazine/design/20tmag-jude-01/20tmag-jude-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/20/t-magazine/design/20tmag-jude-01/20tmag-jude-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/20/t-magazine/design/20tmag-jude-01/20tmag-jude-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge'