Or, at least it bloomed this year. A few hours after I admired it, a freezing, torrential downpour battered the newly flowered branches. A few days before, I woke up to discover not a white tree but a white world, as a springtime blizzard bore down on New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/21/opinion/21englander2/merlin_136894530_9ff843a6-1640-4fe9-a566-ef6497db529c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 580, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/21/opinion/21englander2/merlin_136894530_9ff843a6-1640-4fe9-a566-ef6497db529c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 580}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/21/opinion/21englander2/merlin_136894530_9ff843a6-1640-4fe9-a566-ef6497db529c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 990, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/21/opinion/21englander2/merlin_136894530_9ff843a6-1640-4fe9-a566-ef6497db529c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1979, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/21/opinion/21englander2/21englander2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/21/opinion/21englander2/21englander2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/21/opinion/21englander2/21englander2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy':