a close — in a two-part extravaganza beginning with “Infinity War” — and Marvel listened.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BURBANK, Calif. — Everything ends, even if it might not feel that way right now for Joe and Anthony Russo. More than a year into the making of “Avengers: Infinity War,” these directing brothers were shuttling around the Walt Disney Studios here one evening in March, putting the finishing touches on their latest superhero blockbuster.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/arts/29AvengersFuture-A/merlin_137103729_cae6a3e0-001c-45c2-8512-626139d16e2e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 494, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/29/arts/29AvengersFuture-A/merlin_137103729_cae6a3e0-001c-45c2-8512-626139d16e2e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 494}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/arts/29AvengersFuture-A/merlin_137103729_cae6a3e0-001c-45c2-8512-626139d16e2e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 842, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/arts/29AvengersFuture-A/merlin_137103729_cae6a3e0-001c-45c2-8512-626139d16e2e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1685, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/arts/29AvengersFuture-A/29AvengersFuture-A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/29/arts/29AvengersFuture-A/29AvengersFuture-A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}