ue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/23/opinion/sexual-abuse-workplace.html', 'snippet': 'A reader writes that putting an end to forced arbitration would shine an even brighter light on the issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/12/opinion/12Fowler/merlin_136715811_0acdcf04-df28-4e7b-910c-66cc98154333-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 346, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/12/opinion/12Fowler/merlin_136715811_0acdcf04-df28-4e7b-910c-66cc98154333-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 346}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/12/opinion/12Fowler/merlin_136715811_0acdcf04-df28-4e7b-910c-66cc98154333-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/12/opinion/12Fowler/merlin_136715811_0acdcf04-df28-4e7b-910c-66cc98154333-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1182, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/12/opinion/12Fowler/12Fowler-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/12/opinion/12Fowler/12Fowler-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/12/opinion/12Fowler/12Fowler-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sexual Abuse in the Workplace', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Abuse in the Workplace', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': '#MeToo Movement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-23T17:09:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/40a3312a-e56e-5f75-95a1-3e77076a8fcf', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40a3312a-e56e-5f75-95a1-3e77076a8fcf'}, {'abstract': 'The colorful Italian fashion house has published an equally vibrant cookbook by the son of its creative director.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/23/dining/missoni-family-cookbook.html', 'snippet': 'The colorful Italian fashion house has published an equally vibrant cookbook by the son of its creative director.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Will your Mother’s Day budget allow for a gift from Missoni, the colorful Italian fashion house? Perhaps if Mom would appreciate a cookbook it will. “The Missoni Family Cookbook” by Francesco Maccapani Missoni, the son of Angela Missoni, the company’s creative director, has just been published. It’s every bit as vibrant as the style for which the 65-year-old house is known. But the operative term is “family.” In assembling the book, Mr. Missoni, a devoted home cook, has collected recipes, photos and memories from his relatives. The recipes are organized by season, starting with spring. Milanese-style asparagus with egg, a summery room temperature minestrone with a fresh tomato topping, green beans and potatoes with pesto and no pasta, and classic bollito misto are some winners: “The Missoni Family Cookbook” by Francesco Maccapani Missoni (Assouline, $50).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerfamily/25burnerfamily-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 579, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerfamily/25burnerfamily-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 579}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerfamily/25burnerfamily-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 988, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerfamily/25burnerfamily-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1975, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerfamily/25burnerfamily-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerfamily/25burnerfamily-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerfamily/25burnerfamily-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Missoni, a Stylish Cookbook', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Peruse: A Recipe Collection With a Dash of Style', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Missoni', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Missoni, Angela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Missoni Family Cookbook (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Missoni, Francesco Maccapani', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-23T17:11:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a88dfc2-1624-5e5b-8d5a-c3ed7d269093', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a88dfc2-1624-5e5b-8d5a-c3ed7d269093'}, {'abstract': 'The chef Laurence Edelman of Left Bank has opened Poulet San Tête (chicken without a head), selling rotisserie heritage-breed chicken for nearby delivery or pickup.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/23/dining/rotisserie-chicken-left-bank-nyc.html', 'snippet': 'The chef Laurence Edelman of Left Bank has opened Poulet San Tête (chicken without a head), selling rotisserie heritage-breed chicken for nearby delivery or pickup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Unlike restaurants that seem to deliver just about anything, whether pizza or whole meals, Laurence Edelman, the chef and an owner of Left Bank, a West Village bistro, has created a dedicated service just for chicken to go. Called Poulet Sans Tête, or chicken without a head, it stars juicy, heritage-breed chicken from a specially built rotisserie, either whole, half or quartered. Rich chicken soup, a salad with chicken, and a chopped “health” salad with cabbage and cucumbers are also on the menu. Delivery for now is limited to a one-mile radius; pickup is in the restaurant: Whole chicken, $21, Left Bank, 117 Perry Street (Greenwich Street), 212-727-1170, pouletsanstete.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerchicken-sub/25burnerchicken-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerchicken-sub/25burnerchicken-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerchicken-sub/25burnerchicken-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerchicken-sub/25burnerchicken-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerchicken-sub/25burnerchicken-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerchicken-sub/25burnerchicken-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerchicken-sub/25burnerchicken-sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chicken to Go in the West Village', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Savor: At a West Village Bistro, It’s Simply Chicken to Go', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edelman, Laurence (Chef)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poultry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Left Bank (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Poulet Sans Tete (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-23T17:14:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c301b3a3-63c2-5ffa-a28f-8fe91093c458', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c301b3a3-63c2-5ffa-a28f-8fe91093c458'}, {'abstract': 'Costas Spiliadis, who owns the Estiatorio Milos restaurants, has opened a small market near his Midtown location before unveiling a larger one in Hudson Yards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/23/dining/mediterranean-market-estiatorio-milos.html', 'snippet': 'Costas Spiliadis, who owns the Estiatorio Milos restaurants, has opened a small market near his Midtown location before unveiling a larger one in Hudson Yards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Costas Spiliadis, the owner of the Estiatorio Milos restaurants, considers the handsome little Mediterranean food market he recently opened near his Midtown location to be just a warm-up. “It’s a trial run for the bigger market we’ll soon be opening in Hudson Yards,” he said. A U-shaped counter encircles the space, with stations for coffee and pastries; yogurt; prepared food to go, including gyros from vertical spits; cheeses; charcuterie; smoked fish; and some sashimi-style fish preparations. Featured specialties include whole roasted legs of lamb to take home and big ring-shaped koulouri biscuits. Shelves hold condiments, mostly Greek but also other imports and some from local artisans: Markato, 125 West 55th Street, 212-247-0500, markatofinefoods.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnergreek-sub/merlin_137078199_d87aa8e6-e008-40ce-8e6f-33056bfcd014-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnergreek-sub/merlin_137078199_d87aa8e6-e008-40ce-8e6f-33056bfcd014-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnergreek-sub/merlin_137078199_d87aa8e6-e008-40ce-8e6f-33056bfcd014-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnergreek-sub/merlin_137078199_d87aa8e6-e008-40ce-8e6f-33056bfcd014-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnergreek-sub/25burnermarkato-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnergreek-sub/25burnermarkato-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnergreek-sub/25burnermarkato-sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking a Mediterranean Market for a Test Drive', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Shop: Market Offers a Taste Of Greek Fare to Come', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Estiatorio Milos (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets and Grocery Stores', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spiliadis, Costas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Markato Fine Foods (Manhattan, NY, Market)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-23T17:18:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8f18ab7-f555-57fd-8e7c-6e135fa7a776', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8f18ab7-f555-57fd-8e7c-6e135fa7a776'}, {'abstract': 'Forget your expectations. A former ceramicist is creating beautiful candies without rounding off the edges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/23/dining/chocolate-truffles.html', 'snippet': 'Forget your expectations. A former ceramicist is creating beautiful candies without rounding off the edges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rounds of chocolate filled with ganache may well define the truffle, but not in the hands of Wendy-Dawn Wintcentsen. A ceramicist-turned-chocolatier, she’s a native of Trinidad now based in Brooklyn, where she fashions square bites layered with chocolate, other flavors, candied fruits and even flowers for some truly beautiful confections that would make a lovely gift for Mom. They look like a mosaic in the box: Truffolettes, $20 to $69 for assortments, truffolie.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerchocolate/merlin_136167297_ec2d5d5b-1eda-409c-a17a-b3af87f57786-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 497, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerchocolate/merlin_136167297_ec2d5d5b-1eda-409c-a17a-b3af87f57786-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 497}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerchocolate/merlin_136167297_ec2d5d5b-1eda-409c-a17a-b3af87f57786-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 849, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerchocolate/merlin_136167297_ec2d5d5b-1eda-409c-a17a-b3af87f57786-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1698, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerchocolate/merlin_136167297_ec2d5d5b-1eda-409c-a17a-b3af87f57786-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerchocolate/merlin_136167297_ec2d5d5b-1eda-409c-a17a-b3af87f57786-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnerchocolate/merlin_136167297_ec2d5d5b-1eda-409c-a17a-b3af87f57786-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_