k': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mahler, Gustav', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernstein, Leonard', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pyongyang (North Korea)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-23T17:25:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00a4f4d4-bc99-53b0-a907-48702a850763', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00a4f4d4-bc99-53b0-a907-48702a850763'}, {'abstract': 'Tabasco Diamond Reserve Sauce looks more like a small bottle of Champagne, and costs just as much.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/23/dining/tabasco-mcilhenny-diamond-reserve.html', 'snippet': 'Tabasco Diamond Reserve Sauce looks more like a small bottle of Champagne, and costs just as much.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tabasco is not just one sauce. These days, there are green, sriracha and scorpion versions, among others. But the fanciest one on the list has just been introduced to celebrate the 150th anniversary of the McIlhenny Company, the producer based on Avery Island, La. Bottled with gold foil and packed in a box to suggest Champagne, it is made from specially selected peppers that are mashed with salt and aged for up to 15 years instead of the usual three, then mixed with sparkling wine vinegar, not the garden variety. The result is thicker and definitely more complex: Tabasco Diamond Reserve Sauce, $34.95 for six ounces, tabasco.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnertabasco-sub/merlin_137271756_2b11d249-aa1e-4c68-95e9-491a00eb9633-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnertabasco-sub/merlin_137271756_2b11d249-aa1e-4c68-95e9-491a00eb9633-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnertabasco-sub/merlin_137271756_2b11d249-aa1e-4c68-95e9-491a00eb9633-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 580, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnertabasco-sub/merlin_137271756_2b11d249-aa1e-4c68-95e9-491a00eb9633-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1160, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnertabasco-sub/25burnertabasco-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnertabasco-sub/25burnertabasco-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/25/dining/25burnertabasco-sub/25burnertabasco-sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'McIlhenny Co. Marks Its 150th Anniversary With Special Tabasco', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Zap: Popping a Cork Over Hot Sauce', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McIlhenny Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sauces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-23T17:31:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1def88f2-ff54-5e2c-9094-7c90e8395517', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1def88f2-ff54-5e2c-9094-7c90e8395517'}, {'abstract': '“Rearview Town,” the Nashville star’s first album since the Las Vegas shooting, debuted at the top of the album chart, pushing Cardi B to No. 2.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/23/arts/music/jason-aldean-rearview-town-billboard-chart.html', 'snippet': '“Rearview Town,” the Nashville star’s first album since the Las Vegas shooting, debuted at the top of the album chart, pushing Cardi B to No. 2.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Rearview Town,” the new album by the country star Jason Aldean — his first since the Route 91 Harvest Festival in Las Vegas in October, when a gunman opened fire as Mr. Aldean was performing — opened at No. 1 on this week’s Billboard album chart, making it the first country No. 1 of 2018.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/24/arts/24billboard/merlin_137008767_84b7e069-d9bf-4173-b707-cae7cad05517-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/24/arts/24billboard/merlin_137008767_84b7e069-d9bf-4173-b707-cae7cad05517-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/24/arts/24billboard/merlin_137008767_84b7e069-d9bf-4173-b707-