w are the Browns, Giants, Jets and Broncos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 2018 N.F.L. Draft will help determine the futures of many a franchise. Nearly as important, it will provide bragging rights for the very best mock drafters. It could be a challenging year: “I think that this is going to be a very, very wild ride when it comes to draft night,” said Bucky Brooks of the NFL Network. Here’s a look at what the top mockers are seeing and saying this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/24/sports/24mock/24mock-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/24/sports/24mock/24mock-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/24/sports/24mock/24mock-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/24/sports/24mock/24mock-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/24/sports/24mock/24mock-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/24/sports/24mock/24mock-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/24/sports/24mock/24mock-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Mock Drafts: Who Will Go in the First Round?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mayfield, Baker (1995- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Darnold, Sam (1997- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allen, Josh (1996- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosen, Josh (1997- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-24T09:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Mather', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mather', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a8537aa-9086-503e-b186-4ee1cee63cb6', 'word_count': 1235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a8537aa-9086-503e-b186-4ee1cee63cb6'}, {'abstract': 'Every bit of news sparks tidy cycles of backlash and anti-backlash — the sound of people who can’t sort out who’s actually winning the argument.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/24/magazine/online-or-in-politics-backlash-is-as-predictable-as-weather.html', 'snippet': 'Every bit of news sparks tidy cycles of backlash and anti-backlash — the sound of people who can’t sort out who’s actually winning the argument.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is it possible that anger qualifies, at this point, as a national pastime? It roils our cultural dialogue, poisons social media and — as is frequently, and somewhat helplessly, observed — it curdles much of our politics into a zero-sum game of tribal loathing. It is the predictable response to almost any new development, significant or otherwise: Whatever happens, someone’s fury will most likely rise to meet it, and in the right conditions, it will gather quickly into an entire campaign of “backlash.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29mag-firstwords-t_CA0/29mag-29firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29mag-firstwords-t_CA0/29mag-29firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29mag-firstwords-t_CA0/29mag-29firstwords-t_CA0-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29mag-firstwords-t_CA0/29mag-29firstwords-t_CA0-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1565, 'width': 1565, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29mag-firstwords-t_CA0/29mag-firstwords-t_CA0-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29mag-firstwords-t_CA0/29mag-firstwords-t_CA0-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29mag-firstwords-t_CA0/29mag-firstwords-t_CA0-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 