ple, We Perform for the Gods’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Thailand, Preserving One of the World’s Oldest Art Forms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sai Yong Hong Chinese Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-photojournalism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-24T09:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malin Fezehai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fezehai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36f09efb-3f4b-5f9e-ae10-e0d452f327e5', 'word_count': 1043, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36f09efb-3f4b-5f9e-ae10-e0d452f327e5'}, {'abstract': 'Most elements of the state visit, largely planned by the East Wing, are meant to symbolically honor the relationship between the United States and France. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/24/us/politics/trump-state-dinner-france.html', 'snippet': 'Most elements of the state visit, largely planned by the East Wing, are meant to symbolically honor the relationship between the United States and France. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'In its preview of Tuesday’s state dinner for President Emmanuel Macron of France and his wife, Brigitte, the White House emphasized that many elements about the visit, largely planned by the East Wing, are meant to symbolically honor the historical relationship between the United States and France, an alliance that dates to the Revolutionary War. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0