fected as well. There is also a small but significant risk that other malignancies may occur in the future as a result of the chemotherapy.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29mag-ethicist/29mag-29ethicist-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1002, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29mag-ethicist/29mag-29ethicist-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1002}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29mag-ethicist/29mag-29ethicist-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 613, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29mag-ethicist/29mag-29ethicist-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1400, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29mag-ethicist/29mag-29ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29mag-ethicist/29mag-29ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29mag-ethicist/29mag-29ethicist-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I’m a 73-Year-Old Cancer Survivor. Can I Accept a Kidney?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I’m a 73-Year-Old Cancer Survivor. Can I Accept A Kidney?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transplants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organ Donation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-25T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c28f15cd-793c-5b00-889b-8c37beeb2cf9', 'word_count': 1463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c28f15cd-793c-5b00-889b-8c37beeb2cf9'}, {'abstract': 'Being locked in a room of puzzles can be therapeutic — especially for couples.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/25/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-escape-rooms.html', 'snippet': 'Being locked in a room of puzzles can be therapeutic — especially for couples.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When my coffin lid was slammed shut and padlocked, I didn’t panic. It was dark, and my wrists were chafing from the handcuffs. Nearby, I could hear my husband, Teddy, scrabbling about in his own coffin, testing to see if his lid was sealed securely (from the sound of it: yes). The air smelled like a warm shoe. Teddy shouted my name, and I shouted back. Entombment did nothing to dull our communication skills. Which, I suppose, would be comforting if I believed in the afterlife.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/magazine/29mag-lor/29mag-lor-articleLarge-v2.jpg