section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/books/26bookking1/26bookking1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 880, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/26/books/26bookking1/26bookking1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 880}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/books/26bookking1/26bookking1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 698, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/books/26bookking1/26bookking1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1396, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/books/26bookking1/26bookking1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/26/books/26bookking1/26bookking1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/26/books/26bookking1/26bookking1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A True-Crime Mystery From the 1950s, Fueled by Racism and Corruption', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tale of Rape, Race and Deceit in 1950s Florida', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Gilbert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Beneath a Ruthless Sun: A True Story of Violence, Race, and Justice Lost and Found (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-25T17:03:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Szalai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szalai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/34c3cea5-6cf3-57e8-b17f-06f257943a29', 'word_count': 1067, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34c3cea5-6cf3-57e8-b17f-06f257943a29'}, {'abstract': 'Ma deserves the best nursing home money can buy. Of course. But is it so wrong to hope there might be a little left over?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/25/nyregion/farewell-my-lovely-inheritance.html', 'snippet': 'Ma deserves the best nursing home money can buy. Of course. But is it so wrong to hope there might be a little left over?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have been interviewing architects for the memorial I plan to build to my inheritance. The site will of course be the grounds of my mother’s nursing home in Westchester, and given her diminishing funds, I fear it will be rather small: The size of a birdhouse, I’m thinking. Not just any birdhouse, a birdhouse for old, infirm birdies, with a special area for art therapy and birdie bingo. Having just written the monthly check for my mother’s medical care, I anticipate I’ll be able to spend as much as $280. I hope, nonetheless, to erect a monument that will equal the Taj Mahal in terms of loss and despair. Goddamn it, I wanted that money.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/nyregion/29MISINFORMED/merlin_137260467_f2dbab61-c4df-468d-91f9-3b6715c8a9a2-art