meeting of the top two teams in the East, and a battle of the best in the West. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/26/sports/hockey/nhl-playoffs-second-round.html', 'snippet': 'The second round, which begins Thursday, features a matchup of longtime rivals, a meeting of the top two teams in the East, and a battle of the best in the West. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sure, the division champion Washington Capitals and the two-time defending Stanley Cup champion Pittsburgh Penguins split their four-game season series, but we’re not talking about the regular season anymore. The playoff history between these teams is much more lopsided. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/sports/27nhlpreview-caps/27nhlpreview-caps-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/27/sports/27nhlpreview-caps/27nhlpreview-caps-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/sports/27nhlpreview-caps/27nhlpreview-caps-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/sports/27nhlpreview-caps/27nhlpreview-caps-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1373, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/sports/27nhlpreview-caps/27nhlpreview-caps-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/27/sports/27nhlpreview-caps/27nhlpreview-caps-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/sports/27nhlpreview-caps/27nhlpreview-caps-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.H.L. Playoff Preview: Penguins and Capitals Get Reacquainted ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nashville Predators', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Penguins', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Jose Sharks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Lightning', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vegas Golden Knights', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Capitals', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Winnipeg Jets', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-26T11:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Knoll', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Knoll', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b5f03eb-e844-55c6-860f-24961fa712cd', 'word_count': 988, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b5f03eb-e844-55c6-860f-24961fa712cd'}, {'abstract': 'With unpalatable characters and a crude style, the film makes robbing a comic book convention seem like a bore.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/26/movies/review-supercon-russell-peters.html', 'snippet': 'With unpalatable characters and a crude style, the film makes robbing a comic book convention seem like a bore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a fading attraction of the comic-book convention circuit, Keith Mahar (Russell Peters) is a regular at Supercon, a fan-driven festival that allows this former child actor to charge fans for his autograph. Relegated to sparsely attended panels for 1980s television, Keith drinks and bellyaches with fellow festival D-listers, Matt (Ryan Kwanten), Brock (Brooks Braselman) and Allison (Maggie Grace). The star of the Supercon convention is Adam King (Clancy Brown), a veteran of a science fiction show akin to “Star Trek” whose ego threatens to overshadow his gigantic Supercon autograph fees. After a confrontation between Keith and King leads the convention’s manager, Gil (Mike Epps, a standout), to remove Keith and his friends from the convention lineup, the group of festival outcasts conspire to rob Supercon.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/arts/27supercon/merlin_136988199_e1ab88ef-3267-4426-82f7-f0bd546319ac-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/27/arts/27supercon/merlin_136988199_e1ab88ef-3267-4426-82f7-f0bd546319ac-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/arts/27supercon/merlin_136988199_e1ab88ef-3267-4426-82f7-f0bd546319ac-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ