udan-aid-workers-abduction.html', 'snippet': 'The humanitarian workers were traveling in a convoy between two cities when they disappeared.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya — Ten relief workers traveling in South Sudan have been abducted by an armed group, the United Nations said on Thursday. The kidnapping underscores the risks to humanitarian aid providers in the war-afflicted African country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '10 South Sudan Aid Workers Are Abducted, U.N. Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Militants in South Sudan Abduct 10 Relief Workers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping and Hostages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-26T15:46:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jina Moore and Megan Specia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Megan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Specia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29b0b73e-36bb-5f77-9c5a-352616ff8b49', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29b0b73e-36bb-5f77-9c5a-352616ff8b49'}, {'abstract': 'In the late 18th century, aspiring doctors, desperate for human bodies to study, would surreptitiously dig up cadavers in nearby graveyards. Riots ensued.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/26/nyregion/when-new-york-medical-students-were-body-snatchers.html', 'snippet': 'In the late 18th century, aspiring doctors, desperate for human bodies to study, would surreptitiously dig up cadavers in nearby graveyards. Riots ensued.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. How did doctors in New York do research on cadavers in the age before refrigeration and embalming fluids?', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/nyregion/29fyi/merlin_137307813_a7328de1-dd04-4998-a546-8ec353d06f90-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 485, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/29/nyregion/29fyi/merlin_137307813_a7328de1-dd04-4998-a546-8ec353d06f90-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 485}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/nyregion/29fyi/merlin_137307813_a7328de1-dd04-4998-a546-8ec353d06f90-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 828, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/nyregion/29fyi/merlin_137307813_a7328de1-dd04-4998-a546-8ec353d06f90-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1656, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/nyregion/29fyi/29fyi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/29/nyregion/29fyi/29fyi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/nyregion/29fyi/29fyi-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When New York Medical Students Were Body Snatchers', 'kicker': 'F.Y.I.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cadavers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Schools', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia College', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-26T15:48:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abeec63f-a2ff-5686-a1bc-f9b24bcdf967', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abeec63f-a2ff-5686-a1bc-f9b24bcdf967'}, {'abstract': 'The generic ballot, the president’s approval rating, recent special elections and a seat-by-seat look all point to a modest edge for Democrats. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/26/upshot/what-to-keep-in-mind-when-thinking-about-the-midterms.html', 'snippet': 'The generic ballot, the president’s approval rating, recent special elections and a seat-by-seat look all point to a modest edge for Democrats. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'With less than 200 days until the midterm elections, Democrats are generally thought to have a slight advantage in the fight for control of the House. That doesn’t mean they are going to prevail. The polls could be wrong, as all should understand by now, and there’s more than enough time for the national political environment to turn in favor of the Republicans. But these four indicators, for now, are consistent with a Democratic edge. Here’s what they are and what they’re telling us.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/upshot/27up-house/merlin_137292807_4cbc0eca-e19f-4760-b6b3-c4927ec8266f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/27/upshot/27up-house/merlin_137292807_4cbc0eca-e19f-4760-b6b3-c4927ec8266f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/upshot/27up-house/merlin_137292807_4cbc0eca-e19f-4760-b6b3-c4927ec8266f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/upshot/27up-house/merlin_137292807_4cbc0eca-e19f-4760-b6b3-c4927ec8266f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1397, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/upshot/27up-house/27up-house-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/27/upshot/27up-house/27up-house-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/upshot/27up-house/27up-house-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Keep in Mind When Thinking About the Midterms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print