e board of the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey officially censured Ms. Turner, calling her conduct “outrageous” and “profoundly disturbing.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Port Authority Censures Former Commissioner Who Berated Police', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Port Authority Rebukes Ex-Official for Berating Police', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turner, Caren Z', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tenafly (NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-26T22:46:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e40d13a-0e5c-5d64-b65b-42a54c94976d', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e40d13a-0e5c-5d64-b65b-42a54c94976d'}, {'abstract': 'If Dr. Ronny Jackson gave sleeping pills to reporters and staff on long flights abroad, he broke the law, a D.E.A. spokesman said. “You could be prosecuted.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/26/health/trump-doctor-ambien.html', 'snippet': 'If Dr. Ronny Jackson gave sleeping pills to reporters and staff on long flights abroad, he broke the law, a D.E.A. spokesman said. “You could be prosecuted.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Trips abroad with the president can be grueling for staff and journalists alike. Long hours, with stops in multiple time zones, are often the norm.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/science/27AMBIEN2/27AMBIEN2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/27/science/27AMBIEN2/27AMBIEN2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/science/27AMBIEN2/27AMBIEN2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/science/27AMBIEN2/27AMBIEN2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/science/27AMBIEN2/27AMBIEN2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/27/science/27AMBIEN2/27AMBIEN2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/science/27AMBIEN2/27AMBIEN2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump’s Doctor Accused of Handing Out Ambien. D.E.A. Calls the Practice Illegal.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Handing Out Ambien: Accepted, but Not Legal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ambien (Drug)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drug Enforcement Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Ronny L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-26T22:47:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c6f489c-c2e9-568c-b3b9-933beb811024', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c6f489c-c2e9-568c-b3b9-933beb811024'}, {'abstract': 'To make her documentary series about The New York Times’s coverage of the president, Liz Garbus spent 15 months as a fly on the newsroom wall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/26/insider/true-story-the-fourth-estate.html', 'snippet': 'To make her documentary series about The New York Times’s coverage of the president, Liz Garbus spent 15 months as a fly on the newsroom wall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two weeks after the 2016 election, President-elect Donald J. Trump was in the middle of making the press rounds and had scheduled a meeting with The New York Times. But on the morning of Nov. 22, The Times learned via Twitter that Mr. Trump was canceling. He claimed that the “failing” New York Times had changed the conditions — “not nice.” The paper held its ground, saying it was the Trump team who had tried to change the rules when he asked that the meeting be off the record, which it had refused. Hours later, the president-elect changed course, tweeting the meeting wa