': 'nyt://article/bbd99b45-1b2b-5f96-8b11-1c89b1612953', 'word_count': 836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbd99b45-1b2b-5f96-8b11-1c89b1612953'}, {'abstract': 'The unusual crossover occurred when Kent Jones, the festival chief, submitted his drama, “Diane,” to the downtown event. He won best narrative feature.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/26/arts/tribeca-film-festival-award-goes-to-new-york-film-festival-director.html', 'snippet': 'The unusual crossover occurred when Kent Jones, the festival chief, submitted his drama, “Diane,” to the downtown event. He won best narrative feature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Tribeca Film Festival is known for its crowd-pleasing programming. The crosstown New York Film Festival has an illustrious history of highlighting foreign and art films. But on Thursday, the two institutions seemed to align when Tribeca gave its top award, for best narrative feature, to Kent Jones, the director of both the New York Film Festival and the drama “Diane.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/arts/27tribeca-winners-item/merlin_137192601_d49b3d1a-b5fa-4a48-b0bd-e801ef95d77a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/27/arts/27tribeca-winners-item/merlin_137192601_d49b3d1a-b5fa-4a48-b0bd-e801ef95d77a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/arts/27tribeca-winners-item/merlin_137192601_d49b3d1a-b5fa-4a48-b0bd-e801ef95d77a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/27/arts/27tribeca-winners-item/merlin_137192601_d49b3d1a-b5fa-4a48-b0bd-e801ef95d77a-s