 dance and \u200bmusic performances that are not on the usual tourist lists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/27/travel/europe-festivals.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to regional and local exhibitions, garden tours, and theater, dance and \u200bmusic performances that are not on the usual tourist lists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s the European Year of Cultural Heritage, an ongoing celebration across multiple countries that includes museum exhibitions; tours of gardens and monuments\u200b; theater, dance and \u200bmusical performances; and the reappearance of many long-running annual festivals. Each event is meant to speak to the theme of European cultural heritage in some form or other, according to the European Commission. To that end, many of the activities aim to be both fun and enriching, and appear to be marketed to Europeans rather than to tourists — all the better for travelers seeking novel experiences with a more intimate, local feeling than the usual must-see attractions. Below, a sampling of more than half a dozen events to enjoy (some even for free), \u200bfrom now through the end of the year. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/travel/06getaway2/merlin_25268177_f5162ea6-87f0-4463-8771-f166a0083d1f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/06/travel/06getaway2/merlin_25268177_f5162ea6-87f0-4463-8771-f166a0083d1f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/06/travel/06getaway2/merlin_25268177_f5162ea6-87f0-4463-8771-f166a0083d1f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': 