lay, “Transfers,” draws on her own life as it follows two poor students pitted against each other for a scholarship to an elite institution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday, Lucy Thurber’s play “Transfers’’ made its debut Off Broadway and proved so popular it quickly received an extended run. The play tells the story of two community college students from the South Bronx — one black, one Hispanic — vying for a scholarship at a prestigious liberal-arts college in the northeast. Ms. Thurber, the Obie-award winning writer of “The Hill Town Plays,” grew up in rural poverty in New England and drew in part on her own experiences navigating the world of higher education. The following conversation took place over lunch and via email; it has been condensed and edited.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/nyregion/29big/29big-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 583, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/29/nyregion/29big/29big-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 583}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/nyregion/29big/29big-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 994, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/nyregion/29big/29big-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1989, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/nyregion/29big/29big-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/29/nyregion/29big/29big-thumbStandard