ery, very dire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So far, “Trust” has shown us that J. Paul Getty Sr. is not exactly what you’d call “good with people,” but his instincts for business are spot on. In this week’s episode, however, those instincts are called into question for the first time. In the final moments of the previous episode, we don’t know if little Paul has survived Primo’s raid at the peaceful farmhouse, when Primo shoots Angelo in the face, and we hear a second shot go off before the episode cuts to black. For about half of this episode, the Gettys believe that Paul Sr.’s paltry counteroffer to the kidnappers’ $17 million demand was a tragic miscalculation — that, for once, Getty’s outsized confidence in his “business” acumen has misled him, only this time the cost was not a barrel of oil but his grandson’s life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/watching/29trust-recap/29trust-recap-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/29/watching/29trust-recap/29trust-recap-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/watching/29trust-recap/29trust-recap-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/watching/29trust-recap/29trust-recap-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/29/watching/29trust-recap/29trust-recap-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 't