e rampages. But did he know what else he shared with the group?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/30/opinion/sex-shame-incels-jihadists-minassian.html', 'snippet': 'The Toronto van attacker was probably familiar with the Islamic State’s vehicle rampages. But did he know what else he shared with the group?', 'lead_paragraph': 'As an instrument for delivering publicity, terrorism clearly works. Or at least it did last week, when the hitherto obscure term “incel” went viral after Alek Minassian drove a truck into a crowd of pedestrians in downtown Toronto. Mr. Minassian, just before carrying out his attack, wrote a post on Facebook in which he proclaimed the arrival of an “incel rebellion.” Standing for “involuntarily celibate,” the term is used as a badge of honor among a fringe online subculture of misogynists who say they hate women for depriving them of sex. So now we know.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/opinion/30cottee/merlin_137325273_638375bd-accb-443a-a93e-236dfa3e5523-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/30/opinion/30cottee/merlin_137325273_638375bd-accb-443a-a93e-236dfa3e5523-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/opinion/30cottee/merlin_137325273_638375bd-accb-443a-a93e-236dfa3e5523-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/opinion/30cottee/merlin_137325273_638375bd-accb-443a-a93e-236dfa3e5523-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/opinion/30cottee/merlin_137325273_638375bd-accb-443a-a93e-236dfa3e5523-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/30/opinion/30cottee/merlin_137325273_638375bd-accb-443a-a93e-236dfa3e5523-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/opinion/30cottee/merlin_137325273_638375bd-accb-443a-a93e-236dfa3e5523-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sex and Shame: What Incels and Jihadists Have in Common', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sex, Shame and Terrorism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Abstinence (Sexual)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toronto, Ontario, Attack (April, 2018)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Minassian, Alek', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-30T09:45:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Cottee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cottee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f1aba8b-c97d-54c9-b1a3-d8bb87558477', 'word_count': 956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f1aba8b-c97d-54c9-b1a3-d8bb87558477'}, {'abstract': 'Social justice movements like Black Lives Matter and #MeToo embody his critical spirit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/30/opinion/karl-marx-at-200-influence.html', 'snippet': 'Social justice movements like Black Lives Matter and #MeToo embody his critical spirit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — On May 5, 1818, in the southern German town of Trier, in the picturesque wine-growing region of the Moselle Valley, Karl Marx was born. At the time Trier was one-tenth the size it is today, with a population of around 12,000. According to one of Marx’s recent biographers, Jürgen Neffe, Trier is one of those towns where “although everyone doesn’t know everyone, many know a lot about many.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/02/opinion/30stoneWeb/merlin_23520832_a4f6afc6-45e6-4d17-ab8f-83961d645cc8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 419, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/02/opinion/30stoneWeb/merlin_23520832_a4f6afc6-45e6-4d17-ab8f-83961d645cc8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 419}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/02/opinion/30stoneWeb/merlin_23520832_a4f6afc6-45e6-4d17-ab8f-83961d645cc8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/02/opinion/30stoneWeb/merlin_23520832_a4f6afc6-45e6-4d17-ab8f-83961d645cc8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1430, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/02/opinion/30stoneWeb/30stoneWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/02/opinion/30stoneWeb/30stoneWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/02/opinion/30stoneWeb/30stoneWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Happy Birthday, Karl Marx. You Were Right!', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Socialism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capitalism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marx, Karl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-30T09:45:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Barker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/94a8022b-5b7e-5f67-95c2-db3387eef8ef', 'word_count': 1321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94a8022b-5b7e-5f67-95c2-db3387eef8ef'}, {'abstract': 'Some hate the jungle, but most find hidden strength and unanticipated freedom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/30/opinion/nature-students-risk.html', 'snippet': 'Some hate the jungle, but most find hidden strength and unanticipated freedom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nature is unscripted and hard to predict. Having recently discovered this reality, Penn State has decided that its 98-year-old, student-led Outing Club shall no longer be allowed to go on outings. Citing the high risk of remote environments and poor cellphone service, the university is recommending that the club restrict its offerings to films and speakers. Students are being funneled into engaging only in previously vetted human constructions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/opinion/30heying/merlin_137431521_488c631e-9273-4687-8425-b11d6409ced7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/30/opinion/30heying/merlin_137431521_488c631e-9273-4687-8425-b11d6409ced7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/opinion/30heying/merlin_137431521_488c631e-9273-4687-8425-b11d6409ced7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/opinion/30heying/merlin_137431521_488c631e-9273-4687-8425-b11d6409ced7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/opinion/30heying/30heying-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/30/opinion/30heying/30heying-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/30/opinion/30heying/30heying-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nature Is Risky. That’s Why Stu