eed oils and beer, he has added sake. “Sake is not easy to understand,” he said. “I’m making it easy.” His new sake for everyday drinking, Easy Cup, is a junmai premium sake made from highly polished rice by Gekkeikan, a centuries-old Japanese company. It’s straightforward, mellow and somewhat floral, making it a fine starter sake and excellent to serve chilled with seafood. It comes in a convenient, picnic-ready resealable glass jar at a modest price: Easy Cup Sake, $19.99 for five 7.1-ounce jars, Grand Cru Wine & Spirits, 570 11th Avenue (43rd Street), 646-682-9278, grandcruny.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/02/dining/02burnersake/02burnersake-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/02/dining/02burnersake/02burnersake-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 315}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/02/dining/02burnersake/02burnersake-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 537, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/02/dining/02burnersake/02burnersake-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1074, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/02/dining/02burnersake/02burnersake-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/02/dining/02burnersake/02burnersake-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 