mbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/01/science/00REDFIELD/28CDC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 889, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/01/science/00REDFIELD/28CDC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/05/01/science/00REDFIELD/28CDC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/01/science/00REDFIELD/28CDC-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'C.D.C. Director’s $375,000 Salary Will Be Cut', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Salary of C.D.C. Director Will Be Cut', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Redfield, Robert R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Human Services Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-04-30T18:46:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pam Belluck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belluck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/648aa924-80f5-5eba-9069-1db35940871e', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/648aa924-80f5-5eba-9069-1db35940871e'}, {'abstract': 'The authors argue that America’s predisposition for favoring small business is not just misguided but has had a pernicious effect.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/04/30/business/dealbook/review-big-is-beautiful-questions-the-virtues-of-small-business.html', 'snippet': 'The authors argue that America’s predisposition for favoring small business is not just misguided but has had a pernicious effect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the few remaining topics about which America’s increasingly polarized populace can seem to agree is the relative virtue of small business. Whether you are a Midwestern populist bemoaning the decline of the family farm, an East Coast realist focused on the role of small firms in driving job creation, a Silicon Valley entrepreneur dreaming of disrupting the status quo or just bitter that your favorite local restaurant was replaced by an Olive Garden, everyone, it seems, has reason to embrace small businesses. In the view of Robert D. Atkinson and Michael Lind, the authors of “Big Is Beautiful: Debunking the Myth of Small Business,” America’s predisposition since the 1970s for favoring the little guy is not just misguided but has had a profoundly pernicious effect on our economy and society.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/01/business/01DB_KNEE/merlin_137529501_710647c8-f3df-41dc-ae46-30754920c309-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/05/01/business/01DB_KNEE/merlin_137529501_710647c8-f3df-41dc-ae46-30754920c309-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/05/01/business/01DB_KNEE/merlin_137529501_710647c8-f3df-41dc-ae46-30754920c309-jumbo.jpg', 'he